                    {
                        "id": "8ac141f8-57ea-4ede-9ac1-a0f461eef179",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient presented with flat topped violaceous papules, thinning of nails and onycholysis. Onycholysis is the separation of the nail plate from the nail bed, which is caused by a disruption of the nail matrix. This disruption can be caused by a variety of conditions, including psoriasis, fungal infections, and trauma.\n\nThe microscopic finding observed in this patient is likely to be a suprabasal split. A suprabasal split is a separation of the nail plate from the nail bed, which is caused by a disruption of the nail matrix. This disruption can be caused by a variety of conditions, including psoriasis, fungal infections, and trauma. The suprabasal split is visible under a microscope as a separation of the nail plate from the nail bed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Suprabasal split.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
