                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Dapsone is a sulfone antibiotic that is used for the treatment of bacterial and fungal infections. It is also used for its immunomodulatory actions in the treatment of certain autoimmune diseases.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the mechanism of action of dapsone?\n2. How does dapsone inhibit bacterial and fungal infections?\n3. How does dapsone exert its immunomodulatory actions?\n\nAnswer:\n1. The mechanism of action of dapsone is the inhibition of dihydropteroate synthase, an enzyme involved in the synthesis of folic acid in bacteria and fungi.\n2. Dapsone inhibits bacterial and fungal infections by interfering with the synthesis of folic acid, which is essential for the growth and survival of these microorganisms.\n3. Dapsone exerts its immunomodulatory actions by inhibiting the production of reactive oxygen species and cytokines, which are involved in the inflammatory response. This makes it useful in the treatment of certain autoimmune diseases.",
