                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes.\n\nThe mechanism of action of dapsone is that it inhibits the synthesis of ergosterol, which is a major component of the cell membrane of fungi and bacteria. By inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol, dapsone disrupts the integrity of the cell membrane, leading to cell death and thus treating the infection.\n\nIn contrast, A) Inhibition of cell wall synthesis is incorrect because dapsone does not inhibit the synthesis of the cell wall, which is a structural component of bacteria and fungi.\n\nC) Inhibition of protein synthesis is incorrect because dapsone does not inhibit the synthesis of proteins, which are essential for the functioning of cells.\n\nD) Competition with PABA in folic acid synthesis is incorrect because dapsone does not compete with PABA in the synthesis of folic acid, which is an essential vitamin for the growth and development of cells.",
