                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Dapsone is an antibiotic that belongs to the class of sulfones. Its primary mechanism of action is through the inhibition of dihydropteroate synthase, an enzyme involved in the synthesis of folic acid. This enzyme is essential for the growth and multiplication of bacteria and some fungi. By inhibiting this enzyme, dapsone prevents the synthesis of folic acid, which is necessary for the production of DNA, RNA, and proteins in these organisms.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Competition with PABA in folic acid synthesis",
                        "answers": [
