                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFor bacterial and fungal infections, dapsone works by inhibiting cell wall synthesis. This is because it interferes with the production of a key component of the cell wall, called peptidoglycan. This prevents the bacteria or fungus from growing and reproducing, thus killing it. \n\nFor immunomodulatory actions, dapsone works by inhibiting ergosterol in cell membranes. Ergosterol is a type of sterol found in the cell membranes of fungi, and by inhibiting it, dapsone can reduce inflammation and modulate the immune system. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes.",
                        "answers": [
