                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what dapsone is. Dapsone is an antibiotic that is used to treat bacterial and fungal infections. It is also used for immunomodulatory actions.\n\nThe mechanism of dapsone for these indications is inhibition of cell wall synthesis. Dapsone inhibits the synthesis of cell walls in bacteria and fungi. This prevents the bacteria and fungi from growing and multiplying. Dapsone also inhibits the synthesis of ergosterol in cell membranes. Ergosterol is a component of cell membranes. By inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol, dapsone prevents the cell membranes from being able to function properly. This leads to the death of the bacteria or fungi.",
