                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about how we would assess for intestinal malabsorption. We want to look for evidence that the intestine is not absorbing nutrients properly. Fecal fat estimation, serum lactose levels, and serum amylase levels are all tests that can give us information about nutrient absorption. The NBT-PABA test is a test for bacterial overgrowth in the intestine, which can cause malabsorption.\n\nThe best test for assessment of intestinal malabsorption is the fecal fat estimation.",
                        "answers": [
