                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: Which of the following is the best test for assessment of intestinal malabsorption?\n\nAnswer: A) Fecal fat estimation.\n\nExplanation: Fecal fat estimation is the best test for assessment of intestinal malabsorption because it measures the amount of fat that is not being absorbed in the intestines. This is the most accurate way to assess malabsorption since it directly measures the amount of fat that is not being absorbed. Serum lactose levels, serum amylase levels, and the NBT-PABA test are not as accurate for assessing malabsorption since they measure other factors that may not be directly related to malabsorption.",
