                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's review what the Bezold-Jarisch reflex is. The Bezold-Jarisch reflex is a reflex that is triggered by a decrease in blood pressure, causing an inhibition of the heart rate and a decrease in the force of contraction of the heart.\n\nSecond, let's look at the answer choices. Serotonin, angiotensin, prostaglandin, and histamine are all hormones or neurotransmitters that can affect the heart rate and force of contraction.\n\nThird, let's look at the scientific literature to determine which of these hormones or neurotransmitters is most closely associated with the Bezold-Jarisch reflex. According to a review of the literature, the Bezold-Jarisch reflex is mediated by histamine. Therefore, the correct answer is D) Histamine.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f4dae065-30f3-4ed3-8400-3db428c3505f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
