                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Bezold-Jarisch reflex is mediated by serotonin.\n\nCritique: The answer is correct, but it lacks an explanation or context about the Bezold-Jarisch reflex and how serotonin mediates it.\n\nReconsidering other options:\nB) Angiotensin - This peptide hormone is involved in regulating blood pressure and fluid balance, but it is not directly related to the Bezold-Jarisch reflex.\nC) Prostaglandin - These lipid compounds have various physiological effects, including inflammation and blood flow regulation, but they are not the primary mediators of the Bezold-Jarisch reflex.\nD) Histamine - This compound is involved in immune responses and acts as a neurotransmitter, but it is not the main mediator of the Bezold-Jarisch reflex.\n\nFinal answer: The Bezold-Jarisch reflex is mediated by serotonin (A). This reflex is a cardiovascular response triggered by the activation of certain receptors in the heart, leading to a decrease in blood pressure and heart rate. Serotonin plays a key role in this reflex by activating specific serotonin receptors, which in turn initiate the reflex response.",
                        "answers": [
