                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Answer: C) Prostaglandin\n\nCritique: The Bezold-Jarisch reflex is a cardiovascular reflex that occurs in response to decreased cardiac output or blood volume. It is characterized by a triad of symptoms including bradycardia, hypotension, and increased respiratory rate. The reflex is thought to be mediated by the release of prostaglandins, which activate receptors in the heart and blood vessels, leading to the observed changes in heart rate and blood pressure.\n\nFinal answer: C) Prostaglandin",
