                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what's happening during a voluntary movement. \n\nFirst, the brain sends a signal to the muscles telling them to contract. \n\nAs the muscles contract, they pull on the bones, which results in a movement at the joints. \n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is located at the junction of the muscle and the tendon, and it monitors the tension in the muscle. \n\nAs the muscle contracts and the tension increases, the Golgi tendon organ sends a signal to the brain telling the muscle to relax. \n\nThis feedback loop ensures that the muscle doesn't contract too much and tear the tendon.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
