                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Research what Golgi tendon organ is and its function.\n2. Understand the meaning of voluntary movements.\n3. Determine the role of Golgi tendon organ during voluntary movements.\n4. Analyze the options given in the question.\n5. Choose the option that aligns with the role of Golgi tendon organ during voluntary movements.\n\nAnswer: D) Tension in the muscle.\n\nExplanation: Golgi tendon organ is a sensory receptor located in the tendons that connect muscles to bones. Its primary function is to detect changes in muscle tension. During voluntary movements, the Golgi tendon organ continuously relays information about the tension in the muscle to the efferent neurons. This information is used to adjust the force and speed of muscle contractions, ensuring that the movement is smooth and controlled. Therefore, option D) tension in the muscle is the correct answer.",
