                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what the Golgi tendon organ (GTO) is and its function in the body.\n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a proprioceptive sensory receptor organ that is located at the junction of a muscle and its tendon. Its primary function is to monitor the tension within the muscle during voluntary movements.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Length of the muscle at rest: This is not the primary function of the GTO. The muscle spindle, another type of proprioceptive receptor, is responsible for monitoring the length of the muscle at rest.\n\nB) Change in angle of joint during motion: This is not the primary function of the GTO. The joint receptors are responsible for monitoring the change in angle of the joint during motion.\n\nC) Change in length of muscle before and after the movement: This is not the primary function of the GTO. The muscle spindle is responsible for monitoring the change in length of the muscle during movement.\n\nD) Tension in the muscle: This is the primary function of the GTO. It continuously relays information about the tension in the muscle to the efferent neurons, which helps in regulating muscle contraction and preventing muscle damage due to excessive tension.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Tension in the muscle",
                        "answers": [
