                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a sensor located at the junction of a muscle and tendon. It monitors the tension in the muscle and sends signals to the brain to indicate when the muscle is contracting too hard. This information is then used by the brain to adjust the level of muscle activity.\n\nIn voluntary movements, the Golgi tendon organ plays an important role in relaying information about the tension in the muscle to the brain. This allows the brain to adjust the level of muscle activity to prevent the muscle from contracting too hard and injuring itself.",
