                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a sensor located at the junction of muscle and tendon. It is responsible for detecting changes in muscle length and tension. When a muscle contracts, the Golgi tendon organ is stimulated and sends a signal to the brain. This signal tells the brain to increase the muscle's tension. The Golgi tendon organ is important because it helps to protect the muscle from injury.",
