                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Golgi tendon organ continuously relays to the efferent neurons the tension in the muscle during voluntary movements.\n\nCritique: The answer is correct, but it could be more concise and directly address the question.\n\nReconsidering other answer options:\nA) Length of the muscle at rest - This is not the primary function of the Golgi tendon organ during voluntary movements.\nB) Change in angle of joint during motion - This is more related to the function of muscle spindles, not the Golgi tendon organ.\nC) Change in length of muscle before and after the movement - This is also more related to the function of muscle spindles, not the Golgi tendon organ.\n\nFinal answer: D) Tension in the muscle",
