                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "D) Tension in the muscle\n\nCritique: The Golgi tendon organ is a sensory receptor located at the junction of the muscle and tendon that is responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension. It relays this information to the efferent neurons, which then adjust the tension in the muscle accordingly. Therefore, option D is the correct answer.\n\nReconsidering the other answer options, option A is incorrect because the Golgi tendon organ does not provide information about the length of the muscle at rest. Option B is incorrect because the Golgi tendon organ does not provide information about the change in angle of joint during motion. Option C is incorrect because the Golgi tendon organ does not provide information about the change in length of muscle before and after the movement.\n\nFinal answer: D) Tension in the muscle.",
