                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is A) PAX-6.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to understand what a congenital cataract is and what the PAX-6 gene is. \n\nA congenital cataract is a clouding of the lens of the eye that is present at birth or develops in the first few months of life. \n\nThe PAX-6 gene is a gene that is responsible for the development of the eyes and other parts of the body. It is known to be involved in the development of congenital cataracts.\n\nTherefore, the gene commonly indicated in congenital cataract is PAX-6.",
