                                "answer": " A) PAX-6.\n\nExplanation: Congenital cataracts are a type of eye disorder that is present at birth. PAX-6 is a gene that is associated with the development of the eye and is commonly indicated in congenital cataracts. Therefore, PAX-6 is the gene that is commonly indicated in congenital cataracts.",
