                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe gene commonly indicated in congenital cataract is PAX-6.\n\nCongenital cataracts are a type of eye disorder that is present at birth. They are caused by a mutation in a gene that affects the development of the lens of the eye.\n\nSub-question 1: What genes are associated with congenital cataracts?\nAnswer: PAX-6, CRYGS-3, LMX-IB, and PITX-3.\n\nSub-question 2: Which gene is most commonly indicated in congenital cataracts?\nAnswer: PAX-6 is the most commonly indicated gene in congenital cataracts.",
