                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nD) Saturation of Oxygen\n\nThe best guide for the management of resuscitation is the saturation of oxygen. This is because oxygen saturation reflects the amount of oxygen that is being delivered to the tissues, which is critical for maintaining organ function and preventing damage. Monitoring oxygen saturation can help guide interventions such as oxygen therapy, mechanical ventilation, and fluid resuscitation. While CVP, urine output, and blood pressure are also important parameters to monitor during resuscitation, they are not as reliable or specific as oxygen saturation in guiding management.",
