                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe best guide for the management of resuscitation is D) Saturation of Oxygen. \n\nResuscitation is the process of restoring life to a patient who has suffered cardiac arrest or respiratory failure. The goal of resuscitation is to restore the patient's vital signs to normal levels. Oxygen saturation is a measure of the amount of oxygen in the blood. It is an important indicator of the patient's overall health and is used to monitor the effectiveness of resuscitation efforts.\n\nTo answer the question, it is important to consider the other options. CVP (central venous pressure) is a measure of the pressure in the large veins of the body, and is not a direct measure of oxygen saturation. Urine output is a measure of the amount of urine produced by the body, and is not a direct measure of oxygen saturation. Blood pressure is a measure of the pressure in the arteries, and is not a direct measure of oxygen saturation.\n\nTherefore, the best guide for the management of resuscitation is D) Saturation of Oxygen.",
                        "answers": [
