            {
                "id": "1348a664-1ccc-422f-a083-91d77cb24b92",
                "ref_id": "",
                "question": "Natural disaster causing maximum deaths",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "Hydrological",
                    "Meterological",
                    "Geological",
                    "Fires"
                ],
                "context": "",
                "cot": [
                    "Ans is 'a' i.e. Hydrological DisasterA \"disaster\" can be defined as 'any occurrence that causes damage, ecological disruption, loss of human life or deterioration of health and health services on a scale stiffly-lent to warrant an extraordinary response from outside the affected community or area'.* A \"hazard\" can be defined as any phenomenon that has the potential to cause disruption or damage to people and their environment. - There are many types of disasters such as eahquakes, cyclones, floods, tidal waves, landslides, volcanic eruptions, fires, snowstorms, building collapse, toxicologic accidents, and warfare, etc.* Hydrological disasters (i.e. floods, tsunamis) are associated with causing a maximum death toll. Geological disasters: includes Eahquakes, Avalanches & Volcanic eruptionsMeteorological disasters: include Cyclones, Tornadoes, Hailstorms, Drought, Heatwaves, Blizzards (Blizzards are severe winter storms characterized by low temperature, strong winds, and heavy snow)."
                ],
                "answer": [
                    "Hydrological"
                ],
                "generated_cot": [
                    {
                        "id": "1348a664-1ccc-422f-a083-91d77cb24b92_0",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what each type of natural disaster could entail. \n\nA hydrological disaster could be something like a tsunami, which could potentially kill many people if they are caught in the open water or near the shore. A meteorological disaster could be a hurricane or tornado, which could also kill many people if they are caught in the open or if their homes are destroyed. A geological disaster could be an earthquake, which could kill people if they are caught in a collapsed building or if a landslide occurs. Finally, a fire could also kill many people if they are caught in the flames or if the smoke inhalation is too much. \n\nSo which natural disaster could cause the maximum number of deaths? It really depends on the circumstances, but it is possible that a tsunami could cause the most deaths because it can affect such a large area and so many people could be caught in the open water or near the shore.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "Hydrological",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "lievin",
                        "date": null,
                        "api_service": "",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-002'}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "1348a664-1ccc-422f-a083-91d77cb24b92_1",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-10",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nFirst, we need to identify the type of natural disaster. \n\nThere are four main types of natural disasters: hydrological, meteorological, geological, and fires. \n\nNext, we need to identify the natural disaster that causes the maximum deaths. \n\nAccording to the World Health Organization, the natural disaster that causes the maximum deaths is floods.",
                        "answers": [
