                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Which type of natural disaster causes the highest number of deaths?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Hydrological disasters involve water, such as floods and tsunamis. These can cause significant damage and loss of life, but may not always result in the highest number of deaths.\n- Meteorological disasters involve weather, such as hurricanes and tornadoes. These can also cause significant damage and loss of life, but again may not always result in the highest number of deaths.\n- Geological disasters involve the earth, such as earthquakes and volcanic eruptions. These can be extremely deadly, as they can cause widespread destruction and loss of life.\n- Fires can be caused by a variety of factors, including natural causes like lightning strikes or human causes like arson. While fires can be deadly, they may not always result in the highest number of deaths compared to other types of natural disasters.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) Geological disasters.",
