                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Define each type of natural disaster.\n\nA) Hydrological disasters are related to water, such as floods, tsunamis, and avalanches.\nB) Meteorological disasters are related to weather, such as hurricanes, tornadoes, and heatwaves.\nC) Geological disasters are related to the Earth's structure, such as earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, and landslides.\nD) Fires are disasters involving uncontrolled burning, such as wildfires and bushfires.\n\nStep 2: Research historical data on death tolls for each type of natural disaster.\n\nA) Hydrological: The deadliest flood in history was the 1931 China floods, with an estimated death toll of 1-4 million people.\nB) Meteorological: The deadliest hurricane was the 1970 Bhola cyclone in Bangladesh, with an estimated death toll of 300,000-500,000 people.\nC) Geological: The deadliest earthquake was the 1556 Shaanxi earthquake in China, with an estimated death toll of 830,000 people.\nD) Fires: The deadliest wildfire was the 1871 Peshtigo Fire in the United States, with an estimated death toll of 1,200-2,500 people.\n\nStep 3: Compare the death tolls for each type of natural disaster.\n\nBased on the historical data, the natural disaster causing maximum deaths is:\n\nA) Hydrological: 1931 China floods (1-4 million deaths)\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) Hydrological.",
