                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which type of natural disaster causes the maximum number of deaths.\n\nStep 2: Define the terms\nA) Hydrological disasters: Disasters related to water, such as floods and tsunamis.\nB) Meteorological disasters: Disasters related to weather and climate, such as hurricanes, tornadoes, and heatwaves.\nC) Geological disasters: Disasters related to the Earth's structure, such as earthquakes and volcanic eruptions.\nD) Fires: Disasters related to uncontrolled burning, such as wildfires and bushfires.\n\nStep 3: Research the impact of each type of disaster\nLook up statistics and data on the number of deaths caused by each type of disaster. This can be done through online research, using reliable sources such as government agencies, international organizations, and scientific studies.\n\nStep 4: Compare the data\nAnalyze the data gathered in step 3 and compare the number of deaths caused by each type of disaster. Determine which type of disaster has caused the most deaths historically.\n\nStep 5: Choose the answer\nBased on the comparison in step 4, select the type of disaster that has caused the maximum number of deaths.\n\nAnswer: C) Geological",
