                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe natural disaster causing the maximum deaths is dependent on the region and the time period being considered. For example, in the United States, floods are the most deadly natural disaster, while in India, heat waves are the most deadly.\n\nTo answer this question, we need to consider the region and time period in question. Let's assume the region is the United States and the time period is the last 10 years.\n\nIn the United States, floods are the most deadly natural disaster, causing an average of 140 deaths per year over the last 10 years. This is more than any other natural disaster, including meteorological (e.g. hurricanes, tornadoes, and thunderstorms), geological (e.g. earthquakes and landslides), and fires. Therefore, the answer is A) Hydrological.",
