                        "cot": "A) Hydrological disasters include floods, which can cause a significant number of deaths.\nB) Meteorological disasters include storms, hurricanes, and tornadoes, which can also cause many deaths.\nC) Geological disasters include earthquakes, tsunamis, and volcanic eruptions, which can cause massive loss of life.\nD) Fires, while destructive, typically do not cause as many deaths as the other categories.\n\nConsidering the potential for massive loss of life, the natural disaster causing maximum deaths would likely be a geological disaster (C). Earthquakes, tsunamis, and volcanic eruptions have historically caused some of the highest death tolls in recorded history.",
                        "answers": [
