                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the term \"high risk infant\"\n2. Analyze each option and determine if it fits the criteria for a high risk infant\n3. Choose the option that fits the criteria\n\nAnswer: \n1. A high risk infant is a baby who has a greater chance of developing health problems or complications compared to a typical infant. These health problems can be due to various factors such as genetics, environment, or medical conditions.\n2. \nA) Working mother - While a working mother may face challenges in balancing work and childcare, it does not necessarily make the infant high risk.\nB) Antenatal preeclampsia - This is a medical condition that can cause high blood pressure and damage to organs in the mother. It can also lead to premature birth and low birth weight, which can make the infant high risk.\nC) Third child - The number of children a mother has does not determine if the infant is high risk.\nD) Twins - Twins are considered high risk infants due to the increased likelihood of premature birth, low birth weight, and other complications.\n\n3. The option that fits the criteria for a high risk infant is D) Twins.",
