                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding which of these options is considered a high-risk infant. Can you help me work through it?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option step by step. First, let's look at option A, a working mother. Do you think that would make an infant high-risk?\n\nStudent: I don't think so, because many mothers work and their infants are not necessarily at a higher risk.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. A working mother does not inherently make an infant high-risk. Now, let's move on to option B, antenatal preeclampsia. Do you know what that is?\n\nStudent: I think it's a condition during pregnancy where the mother has high blood pressure and it can cause complications for the baby.\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's right. Antenatal preeclampsia is a pregnancy complication characterized by high blood pressure and potential damage to other organ systems, most often the liver and kidneys. It can lead to premature birth and low birth weight, which can put the infant at a higher risk. So, would you consider this option as a high-risk infant?\n\nStudent: Yes, I think so.\n\nProfessor: Great! Now let's look at option C, the third child. Do you think that would make an infant high-risk?\n\nStudent: I don't see why it would, unless there are other factors involved.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. The birth order of a child does not inherently make them high-risk. Finally, let's consider option D, twins. What do you think about this one?\n\nStudent: I think twins might be considered high-risk because they often have lower birth weights and can be born prematurely.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Twins are often considered high-risk infants due to the increased likelihood of premature birth and low birth weight, as well as other potential complications during pregnancy and delivery. So, based on our discussion, which option would you choose as the correct answer?\n\nStudent: I would choose options B and D, antenatal preeclampsia and twins, as high-risk infants.\n\nProfessor: Well done! You've worked through each option and arrived at the correct answer. Keep up the good work!",
