                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of a high risk infant. A high risk infant is an infant who is at an increased risk of developing health problems due to certain factors.\n\nStep 2: Review the options.\nA) Working mother: This is not considered a high risk infant.\nB) Antenatal preeclampsia: This is considered a high risk infant, as it increases the risk of complications during pregnancy and delivery.\nC) Third child: This is not considered a high risk infant.\nD) Twins: This is considered a high risk infant, as twins are at an increased risk of complications during pregnancy and delivery.\n\nAnswer: B) Antenatal preeclampsia and D) Twins are considered as high risk infants.",
