                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA high risk infant is defined as an infant who is at an increased risk of developing health problems due to certain factors.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What factors can increase the risk of health problems in an infant?\n2. Does any of the given options (A-D) increase the risk of health problems in an infant?\n\nAnswer: B) Antenatal preeclampsia.\n\nAntenatal preeclampsia is a condition that can occur during pregnancy and is characterized by high blood pressure and protein in the urine. It can increase the risk of health problems in an infant, such as low birth weight, preterm birth, and stillbirth. Therefore, antenatal preeclampsia is considered as a high risk infant. The other options (A, C, and D) do not increase the risk of health problems in an infant and are not considered as high risk infants.",
