                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Which sampling method is used to select patients based on potential factors that may impact the results?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Systematic random sampling involves selecting every nth patient from a list, without considering any specific factors.\n- Simple random sampling involves randomly selecting patients from a list, without considering any specific factors.\n- Cluster sampling involves selecting groups of patients based on their location or other shared characteristics, without considering individual factors.\n- Stratified random sampling involves dividing patients into subgroups based on specific factors (such as age or gender), and then randomly selecting patients from each subgroup.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) Stratified random sampling.",
