                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Systematic random sampling is a method where every nth individual is selected from a list or population. This method does not specifically account for potential factors that will affect the results.\n\nB) Simple random sampling is a method where each individual in the population has an equal chance of being selected. This method also does not specifically account for potential factors that will affect the results.\n\nC) Stratified random sampling is a method where the population is divided into subgroups (strata) based on certain characteristics, and then individuals are randomly selected from each subgroup. This method is used to ensure that the sample represents the population with respect to potential factors that will affect the results.\n\nD) Cluster sampling is a method where the population is divided into clusters, and then a random sample of clusters is selected. This method does not specifically account for potential factors that will affect the results.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Stratified random sampling.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
