                    {
                        "id": "7a4d9965-15e2-476a-b151-79c250e87b84",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Altered sensorium refers to a change in mental status, such as confusion, disorientation, or unconsciousness. It can be caused by a variety of medical conditions, including infections, metabolic disorders, and head injuries.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of a complete blood count (CBC)?\n2. Why might a random blood sugar test be ordered for a patient with altered sensorium?\n3. What is the purpose of a lumbar puncture?\n4. Why might a non-contrast CT head be ordered for a patient with altered sensorium?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A CBC is a blood test that measures various components of the blood, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. It can help diagnose conditions such as infections, anemia, and leukemia. However, it may not be necessary for all patients with altered sensorium, as the cause may not be related to blood abnormalities.\n2. A random blood sugar test measures the level of glucose in the blood at a single point in time. It can help diagnose diabetes or monitor blood sugar levels in patients with diabetes. It may be ordered for a patient with altered sensorium to rule out hypoglycemia (low blood sugar) as a cause of the symptoms.\n3. A lumbar puncture, also known as a spinal tap, involves inserting a needle into the lower back to collect cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) for analysis. It can help diagnose conditions such as meningitis, encephalitis, and multiple sclerosis. However, it may not be necessary for all patients with altered sensorium, as the cause may not be related to CSF abnormalities.\n4. A non-contrast CT head is a type of imaging test that uses X-rays to create detailed images of the brain. It can help diagnose conditions such as bleeding, tumors, and stroke. It is often ordered for patients with altered sensorium to rule out serious conditions that require immediate treatment. Therefore, the answer to the original question is C) Lumbar puncture, as it may not be necessary for all patients with altered sensorium.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c275b6c7-87a5-4245-b607-192af7ed9c03",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Lumbar puncture.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
