                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how the Human Development Index (HDI) is calculated?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the HDI is calculated based on three factors: life expectancy, education, and income. \n\nStudent: How is education measured in the HDI calculation?\n\nProfessor: Education is measured by two factors: gross enrollment and adult literacy. Gross enrollment only considers secondary education, not primary education. Two-thirds of the weightage is given to gross enrollment, and one-third is given to adult literacy.\n\nStudent: What about the country's achievement in education?\n\nProfessor: The country's achievement in education is computed based on adult literacy. \n\nStudent: So, which of the following statements is not true regarding the calculation of HDI?\n\nProfessor: The statement that is not true is A) In gross enrollment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education. In fact, both primary and secondary education are considered in gross enrollment.",
