                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question and the concept of HDI\nThe question asks us to identify the statement that is NOT true regarding the calculation of the Human Development Index (HDI). HDI is a composite index that measures a country's average achievements in three basic aspects of human development: health, education, and income.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each statement\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy\n\nStep 3: Recall the components of HDI calculation\n1. Health: Life expectancy at birth\n2. Education: Mean years of schooling and expected years of schooling\n3. Income: Gross National Income (GNI) per capita\n\nStep 4: Compare the statements with the components of HDI calculation\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education - This statement is incorrect because both primary and secondary education are considered in the calculation of HDI.\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy - This statement is true because adult literacy is one of the three components of HDI, and each component is given equal weightage.\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment - This statement is true because gross enrolment is a part of the education component, which is given equal weightage with the other two components.\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy - This statement is true because adult literacy is one of the three components of HDI, and each component is used to compute a country's achievement.\n\nAnswer: The statement that is NOT true regarding the calculation of HDI is A) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.",
                        "answers": [
