                    {
                        "id": "be7a0bc9-3449-4029-b785-0851018bdd0e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which statement is not true regarding the calculation of HDI, let's first understand what HDI is and how it is calculated.\n\nHDI stands for Human Development Index, which is a composite index that measures a country's average achievements in three basic aspects of human development: health, education, and income. The HDI is calculated using the following indicators:\n\n1. Life expectancy at birth (for health)\n2. Mean years of schooling and expected years of schooling (for education)\n3. Gross National Income per capita (for income)\n\nNow let's analyze each statement:\n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\n\nThis statement is not true. In the calculation of HDI, both primary and secondary education are considered. The education component of HDI is measured using mean years of schooling (for adults) and expected years of schooling (for children). Gross enrolment ratio is not used in the calculation of HDI.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy.\n\nThis statement is also not true. Adult literacy is not used in the calculation of HDI. Instead, mean years of schooling is used as an indicator for the education component of HDI.\n\nC) 2/3rd weightage is given to gross enrolment.\n\nThis statement is not true. As mentioned earlier, gross enrolment ratio is not used in the calculation of HDI. The education component of HDI is measured using mean years of schooling and expected years of schooling.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.\n\nThis statement is not true. As mentioned earlier, adult literacy is not used in the calculation of HDI. Instead, mean years of schooling is used as an indicator for the education component of HDI.\n\nTherefore, all of the statements (A, B, C, and D) are not true regarding the calculation of HDI.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d85c8ba7-2fb4-44e6-97f0-fa776e739dd7",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
