                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Human Development Index (HDI) is a composite statistic that measures a country's average achievements in three basic aspects of human development: health, education, and income. It was developed by the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and is used as a tool to rank countries based on their level of human development.\n\nTo answer the question, we need to understand the components of HDI and their respective weightages. The HDI is calculated using the following three indicators:\n\n1. Life expectancy at birth (health)\n2. Education, which is a combination of adult literacy rate and gross enrollment ratio (education)\n3. Gross National Income per capita (income)\n\nNow, let's address each statement:\n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\n\nFalse. Gross enrolment ratio considers primary, secondary, and tertiary education. It is calculated as the total enrollment in a specific level of education, regardless of age, expressed as a percentage of the eligible official school-age population corresponding to the same level of education in a given school year.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy.\n\nTrue. In the education component of HDI, adult literacy rate is given a weightage of 1/3.\n\nC) 2/3 weightage is given to gross enrolment.\n\nTrue. In the education component of HDI, gross enrolment ratio is given a weightage of 2/3.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.\n\nFalse. A country's achievement in HDI is computed based on all three components: life expectancy at birth, education (which includes adult literacy and gross enrolment ratio), and Gross National Income per capita. Adult literacy is just one part of the education component.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is that all of the following statements are true regarding the calculation of HDI except statement A.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "aa874916-6910-4b6d-bbd7-378efb77d491",
