                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding the calculation of the Human Development Index (HDI). Can you help me work through this question?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's look at the statements one by one and see which one is not true regarding the calculation of HDI.\n\nStudent: Okay, let's start with statement A: \"In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\"\n\nProfessor: That statement is incorrect. Gross enrolment considers both primary and secondary education, as well as tertiary education. So, statement A is the exception.\n\nStudent: I see. What about statement B: \"1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy\"?\n\nProfessor: That statement is true. In the calculation of the Education Index, which is a part of HDI, adult literacy is given a weightage of 1/3.\n\nStudent: Alright. And statement C: \"2/3rd weightage is given to gross enrolment\"?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's also true. In the Education Index, gross enrolment is given a weightage of 2/3.\n\nStudent: Lastly, statement D: \"Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.\"\n\nProfessor: This statement is true as well, but it's important to note that it's not the only factor. A country's achievement in the Education Index is computed based on both adult literacy and gross enrolment.\n\nStudent: So, the correct answer is statement A, as it's the only one that's not true regarding the calculation of HDI.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! Well done. Do you have any other questions about HDI?\n\nStudent: No, I think I understand it better now. Thank you for your help, Professor!\n\nProfessor: You're welcome! Don't hesitate to ask if you have any more questions in the future.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0021666e-ef05-484c-8a15-48b71528dc90",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
