                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of HDI. HDI stands for Human Development Index and is a measure of a country's overall achievement in three basic dimensions of human development: health, education, and living standards.\n\nStep 2: Review the four statements and determine which one does not accurately reflect the calculation of HDI.\n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education - This statement is true. Primary education is considered in the calculation of HDI.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy - This statement is true. Adult literacy is given a 1/3 weightage in the calculation of HDI.\n\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment - This statement is true. Gross enrolment is given a 2/3 weightage in the calculation of HDI.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy - This statement is false. Country's achievement is not computed on the basis of adult literacy. It is computed on the basis of health, education, and living standards.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.",
                        "answers": [
