                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant\n\nThe first step in treating an avulsed tooth is to clean the root surface with saline to remove any debris or contaminants. After cleaning, the tooth should be reimplanted as soon as possible to increase the chances of success. Option B involves curetting the root surface, which may cause damage to the root and decrease the chances of success. Option C involves performing a root canal treatment, which is not necessary in all cases of avulsion. Option D involves scrubbing the root surface, which may also cause damage to the root. Therefore, option A is the most appropriate treatment for an 8-year-old child with an avulsed tooth.",
