                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) To determine outliers.\n\nThe Q test is a statistical test used to determine if a data point is an outlier or not. It is used to identify extreme values that are significantly different from the other values in the data set. The Q test is based on the assumption that the data follows a normal distribution. The test compares the size of the difference between a data point and its nearest neighbor to the expected size of the difference based on the number of data points in the set. If the difference is larger than expected, the data point is considered an outlier. Therefore, option B is the correct answer.",
