                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Statistical tests are used to analyze data and draw conclusions about a population based on a sample. The Q test is a statistical test used to determine if a data point is an outlier or not.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is an outlier?\n2. How does the Q test determine outliers?\n3. What is the significance of identifying outliers in data analysis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An outlier is a data point that is significantly different from the other data points in a sample or population.\n2. The Q test determines outliers by comparing the difference between a data point and the median of the sample to the range of the sample. If the difference is greater than a certain value, the data point is considered an outlier.\n3. Identifying outliers is significant in data analysis because they can skew the results and lead to incorrect conclusions. Removing outliers can improve the accuracy of statistical analysis. \n\nAnswer to original question: B) To determine outliers.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c3f3771d-552f-40b4-9bd8-03dada59d714",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
