                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify what lactic acidosis is and how it is caused by Metformin.\n2. Understand the factors that increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\n3. Evaluate each option and determine which one does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nAnswer: B) Smoking\n\nExplanation:\n1. Lactic acidosis is a condition where there is an excess buildup of lactic acid in the body. Metformin can cause lactic acidosis by inhibiting the liver's ability to clear lactate from the blood.\n2. The factors that increase the risk of lactic acidosis include advanced age, liver dysfunction, and renal failure. Advanced age can decrease the body's ability to clear lactate, while liver dysfunction and renal failure can impair the liver and kidneys' ability to remove lactate from the blood.\n3. Option B, smoking, does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis. While smoking can have negative effects on the body, it does not directly impact lactate levels or the liver and kidney's ability to remove lactate. Therefore, the correct answer is B) Smoking.",
