                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which of the given factors does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis, a severe side effect of Metformin.\n\nStep 2: Review each factor\nA) Advanced age: Older individuals may have decreased kidney function, which can increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\nB) Smoking: Smoking can cause various health issues, but it is not directly related to lactic acidosis.\nC) Liver dysfunction: The liver plays a role in clearing lactate from the body, so liver dysfunction can increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\nD) Renal failure: Kidneys help clear lactate from the body, so renal failure can increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nStep 3: Identify the factor that does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis\nBased on the review of each factor, smoking (B) does not directly increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nAnswer: B) Smoking",
                        "answers": [
