                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: Which of the following factors does NOT increase the risk of lactic acidosis caused by metformin?\n\nAnswer: A) Advanced age\n\nReasoning: Lactic acidosis is caused by an accumulation of lactic acid in the body, which is a result of an impaired ability to metabolize glucose. Advanced age does not directly increase the risk of lactic acidosis, whereas smoking, liver dysfunction, and renal failure can all impair the body's ability to metabolize glucose, thus increasing the risk of lactic acidosis.",
