                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nHepatic first pass metabolism is the metabolism of a drug by the liver before it reaches the general circulation. The liver is the main site of drug metabolism and the first pass effect is the reduction in bioavailability of a drug due to its metabolism by the liver. The routes of drug administration that bypass the liver and avoid first pass metabolism are intravenous, sublingual, and intradermal. Oral administration does not bypass the liver and first pass metabolism does occur.",
