                        "cot": " \n\nFirst pass metabolism is when a drug is metabolized by the liver before it enters the general circulation. \n\nOral administration of a drug will go through first pass metabolism because it will be metabolized by the liver before it enters the general circulation. \n\nIntravenous administration of a drug will bypass first pass metabolism because it goes directly into the general circulation. \n\nSublingual administration of a drug will bypass first pass metabolism because it goes directly into the general circulation. \n\nIntradermal administration of a drug will go through first pass metabolism because it will be metabolized by the liver before it enters the general circulation.",
