                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: I'm not sure which enzyme deficiency is causing hypoglycemia in this patient. Could you help me work it out?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Let's start with the symptoms the person is experiencing. They have weakness, fatigue, and hypoglycemia. Hypoglycemia is low blood sugar, so we know that there is a problem with glucose metabolism.\n\nStudent: So, we're looking for an enzyme that is involved in glucose metabolism?\n\nProfessor: Yes. More specifically, we're looking for an enzyme that is involved in the conversion of glucose to energy.\n\nStudent: I see. So, we're looking for an enzyme that is involved in the conversion of glucose to energy.\n\nProfessor: That's right. And we know that the person is taking vitamin tablets, so we can rule out vitamin deficiency as a cause of the hypoglycemia.\n\nStudent: So, we're looking for an enzyme that is involved in the conversion of glucose to energy and is not affected by vitamin deficiency.\n\nProfessor: That's right. Based on those criteria, the most likely enzyme deficiency causing hypoglycemia in this patient is glycogen phosphorylase.",
