                        "cot": "\nThe patient is presenting with hypoglycemia, which is a condition characterized by low blood sugar levels. To determine which enzyme deficiency is causing the hypoglycemia, we need to look at the patient's symptoms and the treatment they received. \n\nThe patient is experiencing weakness, fatigue, and hypoglycemia after consuming raw eggs. This suggests that the patient may have a deficiency in an enzyme that is involved in the digestion of proteins. The doctor gave the patient vitamin tablets, which suggests that the patient may have a deficiency in an enzyme involved in the metabolism of vitamins. \n\nBased on this information, the enzyme deficiency causing the hypoglycemia is likely D) Glucose 6 phosphatase. Glucose 6 phosphatase is an enzyme involved in the metabolism of vitamins, and a deficiency in this enzyme can lead to hypoglycemia.",
