                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient is experiencing hypoglycemia, which is a condition characterized by low blood sugar levels. This can be caused by a number of different enzyme deficiencies, so it is important to narrow down the possibilities. \n\nFirst, it is important to consider the patient's symptoms. Weakness, fatigue, and hypoglycemia are all symptoms of a deficiency in glucose metabolism. This suggests that the enzyme deficiency causing the hypoglycemia is related to glucose metabolism. \n\nNext, it is important to consider the treatment the doctor gave the patient. Vitamin tablets are often used to treat deficiencies in vitamins and minerals, which suggests that the enzyme deficiency causing the hypoglycemia is related to a vitamin or mineral. \n\nBased on this information, the enzyme deficiency causing the hypoglycemia is likely to be D) Glucose 6 phosphatase. Glucose 6 phosphatase is an enzyme involved in glucose metabolism and is often deficient in patients with hypoglycemia. Vitamin tablets are often used to treat deficiencies in this enzyme.",
