                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What could be causing the hypoglycemia in this patient?\n\nProfessor: The patient is likely suffering from an enzyme deficiency, which is causing the hypoglycemia. The four possible enzyme deficiencies are: A) Phosphoenol pyruvate carboxykinase, B) Pyruvate carboxylase, C) Glycogen phosphorylase, and D) Glucose 6 phosphatase. \n\nStudent: How do I know which one is causing the hypoglycemia?\n\nProfessor: To determine which enzyme deficiency is causing the hypoglycemia, you need to look at the symptoms the patient is presenting with. In this case, the patient is presenting with weakness, fatigue, and hypoglycemia. Based on these symptoms, the most likely enzyme deficiency causing the hypoglycemia is Glucose 6 Phosphatase.",
                        "answers": [
