                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) Remove when presbyopia sets in.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we must first understand what an IOL is. An IOL is an intraocular lens, which is a type of lens that is surgically implanted into the eye to replace the eye's natural lens. It is typically used to correct vision problems such as nearsightedness, farsightedness, and astigmatism.\n\nNow that we understand what an IOL is, we can look at the question. The question states that an IOL has been placed in a young male and asks what should be done after 10 years.\n\nThe answer is C) Remove when presbyopia sets in. Presbyopia is a condition that affects people over the age of 40, where the eye's lens becomes less flexible and the ability to focus on close objects decreases. Therefore, if the IOL was placed in a young male, it is unlikely that presbyopia will have set in after 10 years. However, it is important to monitor the IOL for any signs of Posterior Capsule ossification, which is a condition where the capsule that holds the IOL in place becomes hardened and can cause vision problems. If this condition is present, then the IOL should be removed. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Remove when presbyopia sets in.",
                        "answers": [
