                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nReformulated question: After 10 years, what should be done with an IOL placed in a young male?\n\nAnswer: A) IOL should be removed in case of Posterior Capsule ossification.\n\nExplanation: An IOL (intraocular lens) is a type of lens implant used to replace the natural lens of the eye. In the case of a young male, the IOL should be monitored for any signs of Posterior Capsule ossification, which is a condition where the capsule of the lens becomes hardened. If this occurs, the IOL should be removed. In the absence of Posterior Capsule ossification, the IOL should not be removed and should remain in place. It should not be changed after 10 years, unless there is a medical reason to do so.",
