                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) First pass effect.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, it is important to understand the definition of each of the terms. \n\nA) Excretion is the process by which waste products of metabolism and other substances that are in excess of body requirements are eliminated from the body.\n\nB) First pass effect is the process by which a drug is metabolized by the liver before entering the systemic circulation.\n\nC) First order elimination is the process by which a drug is eliminated from the body at a constant rate.\n\nD) Metabolism is the process by which a drug is broken down into smaller molecules by enzymes in the body.\n\nGiven the definition of each of the terms, it is clear that the process by which the amount of a drug in the body decreases after administration, but before entering the systemic circulation is B) First pass effect.",
