                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Piaget's theory of cognitive development includes four stages: sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, and formal operational. The preoperational stage is the second stage and occurs between the ages of 2 and 7.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is Piaget's theory of cognitive development?\nPiaget's theory of cognitive development includes four stages: sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, and formal operational. \n\n2. What is the preoperational stage?\nThe preoperational stage is the second stage of Piaget's theory of cognitive development and occurs between the ages of 2 and 7. \n\n3. What are the characteristics of the preoperational stage?\nThe characteristics of the preoperational stage include egocentrism, animism, centration, and lack of conservation. \n\n4. What is the period of the preoperational stage according to Piaget?\nThe period of the preoperational stage according to Piaget is 2-7 years. \n\nAnswer: C) 2-6 years.",
