                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand what each option means.\n2. Determine which option is most appropriate for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n3. Choose the correct option.\n\nAnswer:\n1. A) Active surveillance: This involves actively seeking out cases of a particular disease or condition.\n2. B) Sentinel surveillance: This involves monitoring a specific group of people who are at high risk for a particular disease or condition.\n3. C) Passive surveillance: This involves relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a particular disease or condition.\n4. D) Routine checkup of all operated cases: This involves regularly checking on all patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nBased on the question, the most appropriate option for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB would be D) Routine checkup of all operated cases. This option ensures that all patients are regularly checked on and any vision effects can be detected and addressed in a timely manner.",
                        "answers": [
