                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the context\n- We are evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB (presumably phacoemulsification with intraocular lens implantation).\n\nStep 2: Define the surveillance methods\nA) Active surveillance: Regularly and proactively collecting data on a specific condition or event.\nB) Sentinel surveillance: Monitoring a select group of reporting sites or individuals to track trends in a specific condition or event.\nC) Passive surveillance: Relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a specific condition or event as they occur.\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases: Regularly examining all patients who have undergone the surgery to assess their outcomes.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most appropriate method\n- In this case, we want to evaluate the vision effects after cataract extraction surgery. Therefore, we need a method that involves regularly examining all patients who have undergone the surgery.\n\nAnswer: D) Routine checkup of all operated cases",
