                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what is being asked. We are being asked to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery. This means that we need to look at the vision of people who have had this surgery and see if there are any effects. \n\nNext, we need to understand what PCB is. PCB is a type of surgery, so we need to look at the vision of people who have had this surgery and see if there are any effects. \n\nFinally, we need to understand what the different types of surveillance are. Active surveillance means that we are actively looking for cases of vision problems after surgery. Sentinel surveillance means that we are looking for cases of vision problems after surgery, but we are only looking for cases that have been reported to us. Passive surveillance means that we are not actively looking for cases of vision problems after surgery, but we will investigate if we hear about them. Routine checkup of all operated cases means that we will check the vision of all people who have had this surgery at regular intervals. \n\nBased on this information, we can see that the best answer is D) Routine checkup of all operated cases. This is the only type of surveillance that will allow us to proactively check the vision of all people who have had this surgery, which is what we need to do in order to evaluate post-operative vision effects.",
