                    {
                        "id": "26de849b-4589-4d37-b88a-c49d292456f5",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Pulmonary compliance is a measure of the lung's ability to stretch and expand. It is calculated by dividing the change in lung volume by the change in transpulmonary pressure.\n\nAdditional facts: The transpulmonary pressure is the difference between the alveolar pressure and the intrapleural pressure.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the change in lung volume?\n2. What is the change in transpulmonary pressure?\n3. What is the formula for pulmonary compliance?\n4. What is the pulmonary compliance in this patient?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The change in lung volume is the tidal volume, which is 500 mL.\n2. The change in transpulmonary pressure is the difference between the alveolar pressure and the intrapleural pressure. The alveolar pressure is atmospheric pressure, which is 0 cm of water. Therefore, the change in transpulmonary pressure is 9 - (-4) = 13 cm of water.\n3. The formula for pulmonary compliance is change in lung volume / change in transpulmonary pressure.\n4. Plugging in the values, we get pulmonary compliance = 500 mL / 13 cmH2O = 0.038 L/cmH2O. However, the answer choices are in L/cm, so we need to convert cmH2O to cm. 1 cmH2O is equivalent to 0.098 kPa, and 1 kPa is equivalent to 10 cm of water. Therefore, 1 cmH2O is equivalent to 0.98 cm. Multiplying the change in transpulmonary pressure by 0.98, we get 12.74 cm. Plugging in the converted values, we get pulmonary compliance = 500 mL / 12.74 cm = 0.039 L/cm. This is closest to answer choice B) 0.3 L/cm. Therefore, the answer is B) 0.3 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c5abd317-b9c6-4be5-ac30-b4ecc9f961b5",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) 0.3 L/cm.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 04:32:39",
