                    {
                        "id": "185c5b7a-c59e-438c-982d-9b7d5aaa72e0",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "zhou-01-ins",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Determine the change in volume and pressure\nThe tidal volume is given as 500 mL, which is equal to 0.5 L. This is the change in volume (\u2206V) during inspiration.\nThe intrapleural pressure before inspiration is -4 cm of water, and after inspiration, it is -9 cm of water. The change in pressure (\u2206P) is the difference between these two values: -9 - (-4) = -5 cm of water.\n\nStep 2: Convert the pressure to the same units\nTo calculate pulmonary compliance, we need to have the pressure in the same units. We can convert cm of water to cm H2O by multiplying by 1.36 (1 cm H2O = 1.36 cm H2O). So, -5 cm of water = -5 * 1.36 = -6.8 cm H2O.\n\nStep 3: Calculate pulmonary compliance\nPulmonary compliance (C) is the change in volume (\u2206V) divided by the change in pressure (\u2206P). So, C = \u2206V / \u2206P = 0.5 L / -6.8 cm H2O.\n\nStep 4: Simplify the result\nC = 0.5 L / -6.8 cm H2O \u2248 0.0735 L/cm H2O.\n\nStep 5: Compare the result to the given options\nThe calculated pulmonary compliance is approximately 0.0735 L/cm H2O. This value is closest to option A) 0.1 L/cm. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\nA) 0.1 L/cm",
                        "answers": [
