                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe tidal volume is the volume of air inhaled or exhaled in a single breath. The intrapleural pressure is the pressure within the pleural cavity.\n\nThe pulmonary compliance is the volume of air that the lungs can expand or contract in a single breath.\n\nThe formula for pulmonary compliance is:\n\nPulmonary compliance = Tidal volume / (Intrapleural pressure after inspiration - Intrapleural pressure before inspiration)\n\nIn this patient, the pulmonary compliance would be:\n\nPulmonary compliance = 500 mL / (-9 cm of water - (-4 cm of water))\n\nPulmonary compliance = 500 mL / (5 cm of water)\n\nPulmonary compliance = 100 mL/cm of water\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
