                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which of the given options does not show optic atrophy.\n\nStep 2: Understand the options\nA) Retinitis pigmentosa - a genetic disorder that causes degeneration of the retina\nB) Methanol poisoning - ingestion of methanol can cause optic nerve damage and blindness\nC) Central retinal aerial occlusion (CRAO) - blockage of the central retinal artery leading to sudden vision loss\nD) Polypoidal choroidal vasculopathy - a type of eye disease that affects the blood vessels in the choroid layer of the eye\n\nStep 3: Eliminate options\nWe know that optic atrophy is a condition where the optic nerve becomes damaged and leads to vision loss. Therefore, we can eliminate options B, C, and D as they all involve some form of optic nerve damage. \n\nStep 4: Final answer\nThe correct answer is A) Retinitis pigmentosa, as it does not involve optic atrophy.",
