                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nQ: A male child with coarse facial features, macroglossia, thick lips presents with copious mucous discharge from nose at 10 months of age. The child was absolutely normal at birth. On examination he was found to have enlarged Liver and Spleen. Diagnosis is:\n\nA) Hurler's syndrome\nB) Beckwith-Weidman syndrome\nC) Hypothyroidism\nD) Proteus syndrome\n\nA) Hurler's syndrome is a disorder that is characterized by the buildup of a substance called heparan sulfate in the body. This can lead to a number of problems, including coarse facial features, macroglossia, thick lips, and copious mucous discharge from the nose.\n\nB) Beckwith-Weidman syndrome is a disorder that is characterized by the enlargement of the liver and spleen. This can lead to a number of problems, including coarse facial features, macroglossia, thick lips, and copious mucous discharge from the nose.\n\nC) Hypothyroidism is a disorder that is characterized by an underactive thyroid gland. This can lead to a number of problems, including coarse facial features, macroglossia, thick lips, and copious mucous discharge from the nose.\n\nD) Proteus syndrome is a disorder that is characterized by the overgrowth of tissues and organs. This can lead to a number of problems, including coarse facial features, macroglossia, thick lips, and copious mucous discharge from the nose.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "ba5dbc00-c680-40c4-87b0-3ae1f3eafe9f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
