            {
                "id": "62e089d3-5425-4349-8edc-3ce132c0bf66",
                "ref_id": "",
                "question": "Which of the following doesn't occur in 5' to 3' direction?",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "DNA repair",
                    "DNA replication",
                    "RNA editing",
                    "Transcription"
                ],
                "context": "",
                "cot": [
                    "The 5' is upstream; the 3' is downstream. DNA and RNA are synthesized in the 5' to 3' direction In DNA Replication whenever synthesis occurs new nucleotide is added to 3' end In transcription, RNA is getting synthesized in 5' to 3' direction RNA editing It occurs in 3'-5' direction Post transcriptional modification in which differential RNA processing occurs. Also called chemical modification of RNA, in which mostly Cytosine gets conveed to Uracil. DNA Replication ,Proof reading DNA Repair 3'-5' exonuclease activity Mostly endonuclease activity, but sometimes it is 5'-3' exonuclease activity."
                ],
                "answer": [
                    "RNA editing"
                ],
                "generated_cot": [
                    {
                        "id": "62e089d3-5425-4349-8edc-3ce132c0bf66_0",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what happens during each of these processes: \n\nDNA repair: DNA is cut at the site of damage and then new DNA is synthesized to fill in the gap. \nDNA replication: DNA is unwound and then new DNA is synthesized to complement the template strand. \nRNA editing: RNA is cut at the site of damage and then new RNA is synthesized to fill in the gap. \nTranscription: RNA is synthesized complementary to the template strand of DNA. \n\nSo, DNA repair and RNA editing both involve cutting and then synthesizing new nucleotides to fill in the gap. DNA replication involves unwinding the double helix, but no cutting occurs. Transcription involves synthesizing new RNA, but no cutting occurs. Therefore, the answer is D.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "Transcription",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "lievin",
                        "date": null,
                        "api_service": "",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-002'}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
