                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the meaning of 5' to 3' direction.\n2. Understand the processes of DNA repair, DNA replication, RNA editing, and transcription.\n3. Determine which process occurs in the opposite direction of 5' to 3'.\n4. Choose the option that matches the process.\n\nAnswer:\n1. The 5' to 3' direction refers to the direction in which DNA and RNA strands are synthesized. It means that the 5' end of the nucleotide is attached to the phosphate group, and the 3' end is attached to the hydroxyl group.\n2. DNA repair is the process of correcting damaged DNA. DNA replication is the process of copying DNA. RNA editing is the process of modifying RNA after transcription. Transcription is the process of synthesizing RNA from DNA.\n3. The process that occurs in the opposite direction of 5' to 3' is transcription. Transcription occurs in the 3' to 5' direction.\n4. Therefore, the answer is D) Transcription.",
