                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Which process does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The 5' to 3' direction refers to the direction in which nucleotides are added to a growing nucleic acid chain.\n- DNA repair involves the removal and replacement of damaged nucleotides, which can occur in either direction.\n- DNA replication involves the synthesis of a new DNA strand in the 5' to 3' direction, using the existing strand as a template.\n- RNA editing involves the modification of RNA molecules after they have been transcribed from DNA, which can occur in either direction.\n- Transcription involves the synthesis of an RNA molecule in the 5' to 3' direction, using a DNA template.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) RNA editing, as it does not necessarily occur in the 5' to 3' direction.",
