                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which of the given processes does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStep 2: Understand the 5' to 3' direction\nThe 5' to 3' direction refers to the direction in which nucleotides are added to a growing nucleic acid chain. In DNA and RNA, nucleotides are added in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStep 3: Analyze each option\nA) DNA repair: DNA repair can occur in any direction and is not specific to the 5' to 3' direction. \nB) DNA replication: DNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, as nucleotides are added to the growing DNA strand in this direction. \nC) RNA editing: RNA editing can occur in any direction and is not specific to the 5' to 3' direction. \nD) Transcription: Transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, as RNA is synthesized in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStep 4: Determine the answer\nBased on the analysis of each option, the answer is option A) DNA repair, as it is not specific to the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStep 5: Verify the answer\nWe can verify the answer by checking if DNA repair occurs only in the 5' to 3' direction. According to research, DNA repair can occur in any direction and is not specific to the 5' to 3' direction. Therefore, the answer is correct.\n\nFinal answer: A) DNA repair.",
