                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Research tetralogy of Fallot and its symptoms.\n2. Determine how different positions affect blood flow and oxygenation in the body.\n3. Analyze which position would be most beneficial for a child with tetralogy of Fallot.\n4. Choose the correct answer based on the analysis.\n\nAnswer:\nTetralogy of Fallot is a congenital heart defect that affects the flow of blood through the heart and lungs. It is characterized by four abnormalities in the heart's structure, including a ventricular septal defect, pulmonary stenosis, an overriding aorta, and right ventricular hypertrophy.\n\nIn tetralogy of Fallot, blood flow to the lungs is restricted, leading to low oxygen levels in the body. To compensate for this, the body may adopt certain positions that improve blood flow and oxygenation.\n\nResearch suggests that squatting is the most beneficial position for children with tetralogy of Fallot. Squatting increases the resistance in the legs, which helps to increase blood flow to the lungs and improve oxygenation. Leaning forwards can also be helpful in improving blood flow to the lungs.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Squatting.",
