                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the symptoms and biopsy results. The patient has pain in the calf muscles on exercise and a biopsy revealed an excessive amount of glycogen present in the muscle. \n\nStep 2: Research the different enzyme deficiencies that could be causing the symptoms and biopsy results. \n\nStep 3: Compare the symptoms and biopsy results to the different enzyme deficiencies. \n\nThe most likely enzyme deficiency is Phosphorylase enzyme (D). This enzyme is responsible for the breakdown of glycogen, which is the excessive amount of glycogen present in the muscle.",
