                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, it is important to note that glycogen is a polysaccharide composed of glucose molecules. It is stored in the muscles and is broken down into glucose molecules when energy is needed.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the role of enzymes in the breakdown of glycogen?\n2. What enzyme is responsible for the breakdown of glycogen into glucose molecules?\n\nAnswer to sub-question 1: Enzymes are proteins that act as catalysts to speed up chemical reactions. In the case of glycogen breakdown, enzymes are responsible for breaking down the polysaccharide into glucose molecules.\n\nAnswer to sub-question 2: The enzyme responsible for the breakdown of glycogen into glucose molecules is phosphorylase enzyme.\n\nTherefore, the most likely enzyme deficiency in the adolescent male patient is phosphorylase enzyme (D).",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e9fe0918-699c-4c04-be48-3b454ee0df40",
