                    {
                        "id": "434dd02a-d6bb-442e-a4f5-95b966948f85",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "refl-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The most likely enzyme deficiency is D) Phosphorylase enzyme.\n\nCritique: The answer provided is correct, as a deficiency in the phosphorylase enzyme would lead to an accumulation of glycogen in the muscle, causing pain during exercise. However, the answer could be more detailed and provide a brief explanation of the role of the enzyme and the resulting condition.\n\nReconsidering other answer options:\nA) Muscle debranching enzyme deficiency would lead to a glycogen storage disease called Cori disease or GSD type III, which primarily affects the liver and muscles. However, this condition is less common and typically presents with hepatomegaly and hypoglycemia, not just muscle pain during exercise.\nB) Phosphofructokinase I deficiency leads to Tarui disease or GSD type VII, which also presents with exercise-induced muscle pain and weakness. However, this condition is rarer than phosphorylase enzyme deficiency.\nC) Glucose 6 phosphatase deficiency leads to von Gierke disease or GSD type I, which primarily affects the liver and kidneys, causing hepatomegaly and hypoglycemia. Muscle pain during exercise is not a typical symptom of this condition.\n\nFinal answer: The most likely enzyme deficiency in this adolescent male patient with pain in calf muscles on exercise and excessive glycogen in muscle biopsy is D) Phosphorylase enzyme. This deficiency leads to McArdle disease or glycogen storage disease type V, which is characterized by exercise-induced muscle pain, cramps, and weakness due to the inability to break down glycogen in the muscles.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d767b4aa-0244-4ef6-8fe8-829ef5da366b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Phosphorylase enzyme.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/17 17:35:37",
