                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the condition described in the question.\nThe patient has pain in calf muscles on exercise, which suggests a muscle disorder.\n\nStep 2: Identify the abnormality found on biopsy.\nThe biopsy showed an excessive amount of glycogen in the muscle.\n\nStep 3: Determine the enzyme involved in glycogen metabolism.\nGlycogen is a complex carbohydrate that is stored in the liver and muscles. It is broken down into glucose by the enzyme glycogen phosphorylase.\n\nStep 4: Identify the enzyme deficiency that could lead to excessive glycogen accumulation in the muscle.\nThere are several enzyme deficiencies that can lead to excessive glycogen accumulation in the muscle. The most common ones are:\n\n- Muscle debranching enzyme deficiency: This enzyme is responsible for breaking down the branches of glycogen molecules. Without it, glycogen accumulates in the muscle.\n- Phosphorylase enzyme deficiency: This enzyme is responsible for breaking down glycogen into glucose. Without it, glycogen accumulates in the muscle.\n- Phosphofructokinase I deficiency: This enzyme is involved in the breakdown of glucose for energy production. Without it, the muscle cannot produce enough energy and glycogen accumulates.\n- Glucose 6 phosphatase deficiency: This enzyme is involved in the release of glucose from glycogen. Without it, glycogen accumulates in the liver and muscles.\n\nStep 5: Choose the most likely enzyme deficiency based on the clinical presentation and biopsy findings.\nThe patient has pain in calf muscles on exercise, which suggests a muscle disorder. The biopsy showed excessive glycogen accumulation in the muscle. This is most consistent with a muscle disorder caused by a deficiency in the phosphorylase enzyme, which is responsible for breaking down glycogen into glucose. Therefore, the correct answer is D) Phosphorylase enzyme.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "27673f0a-a992-434e-b926-d1bd284a4cf8",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Phosphorylase enzyme.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
