                        "cot": " The patient has pain in calf muscles on exercise. This suggests that the muscles are not getting enough energy. Where does energy come from? Glucose. So there must be something wrong with the way the muscle is metabolizing glucose.\n\nThe biopsy showed that there was an excessive amount of glycogen present. This means that the muscle is not able to break down glycogen into glucose. The most likely enzyme deficiency is phosphorylase, which is responsible for breaking down glycogen into glucose.",
