                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: Which city had the highest amount of water vapor in the air during our trip?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. We need to determine the humidity levels in each city to understand which one had more water vapor in the air.\n2. We can assume that higher humidity levels indicate more water vapor in the air.\n\nLet's analyze each city:\n\nA) Hanoi: This city is located in Vietnam, which has a tropical climate. Tropical climates are known for their high humidity levels, so Hanoi likely has a significant amount of water vapor in the air.\n\nB) Athens: This city is located in Greece, which has a Mediterranean climate. Mediterranean climates are known for their warm, dry summers and mild, wet winters. The humidity levels in Athens may vary depending on the season, but overall, it is not as humid as a tropical climate.\n\nC) Baghdad: This city is located in Iraq, which has a desert climate. Desert climates are known for their low humidity levels, so Baghdad likely has less water vapor in the air compared to the other cities.\n\nD) Phoenix: This city is located in the United States, specifically in Arizona, which also has a desert climate. Like Baghdad, Phoenix likely has low humidity levels and less water vapor in the air compared to the other cities.\n\nBased on this analysis, the city with the most water vapor in the air during our trip is:\n\nA) Hanoi",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "2ca39218-d07e-4699-a7e1-2026c899fe36",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Hanoi.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
