                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: In which type of environment are seals most likely to be found?\nOptions: \nA) desert\nB) arctic\nC) Mediterranean\nD) tropical\n\nStep 1: Let's consider each option and think about the characteristics of each environment and whether seals would be likely to inhabit them.\n\nA) Desert - Deserts are characterized by extremely dry conditions and a lack of water. Seals are marine mammals that rely on water for their survival, so it is unlikely that they would be found in a desert environment.\n\nB) Arctic - The Arctic is a cold, icy environment that is home to a variety of marine life. Seals are known to inhabit cold waters and rely on ice for resting and breeding. This environment seems like a suitable habitat for seals.\n\nC) Mediterranean - The Mediterranean is a region with a mild climate and relatively warm waters. While some species of seals, such as the Mediterranean monk seal, can be found in this region, it is not the most common environment for seals in general.\n\nD) Tropical - Tropical environments are characterized by warm temperatures and abundant rainfall. Although some species of seals can be found in warmer waters, the majority of seals are adapted to colder environments.\n\nStep 2: Based on our analysis of each environment, it seems that the arctic environment (option B) is the most likely habitat for seals in general. While some species can be found in other environments, the majority of seals are adapted to cold waters and rely on ice for resting and breeding.\n\nAnswer: B) Arctic",
