                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Seals are marine mammals that belong to the family Phocidae. They are primarily found in cold and temperate waters, although some species can be found in warmer regions as well. To determine the type of environment where seals are most likely to be found, we need to consider the habitats of different seal species.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) What are the different species of seals and their habitats?\n2) Which of the given environments best matches the habitats of most seal species?\n\n1) There are around 33 species of seals, and they can be found in various regions across the world. Some common species and their habitats include:\n- Harbor seals: found in temperate coastal waters of the North Atlantic and North Pacific Oceans.\n- Grey seals: found in the North Atlantic Ocean, particularly around the coasts of the UK, Canada, and the northeastern United States.\n- Harp seals: found in the Arctic and North Atlantic Oceans.\n- Weddell seals: found in the Antarctic region.\n- Mediterranean monk seals: found in the Mediterranean Sea and the eastern Atlantic Ocean.\n- Hawaiian monk seals: found in the Hawaiian Islands, which are in a tropical region.\n\n2) Comparing the given environments with the habitats of different seal species:\nA) Desert: Seals are marine mammals and are not found in desert environments.\nB) Arctic: Many seal species, such as harp seals and Weddell seals, are found in the Arctic and Antarctic regions.\nC) Mediterranean: Mediterranean monk seals are found in this region, but they are one of the rarest seal species.\nD) Tropical: Hawaiian monk seals are found in the tropical region, but they are also a rare species.\n\nBased on the information above, seals are most likely to be found in the Arctic environment (option B), as many species are adapted to live in cold and temperate waters.",
                        "answers": [
