                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the process of decaying vegetation.\nDecaying vegetation is the process where dead plant material breaks down and decomposes, releasing nutrients back into the soil and atmosphere.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each option in relation to decaying vegetation.\n\nA) Enables nuclear power to function\nNuclear power relies on nuclear reactions, specifically the splitting of atoms, to produce energy. This process is not related to decaying vegetation.\n\nB) Enables the emitting of light beams\nThe emitting of light beams is a result of energy transitions in atoms or molecules, which is not directly related to decaying vegetation.\n\nC) Enables gas-powered motors to operate\nGas-powered motors rely on the combustion of fossil fuels, such as gasoline, to produce energy. While fossil fuels are formed from the remains of ancient plants and animals, decaying vegetation itself does not directly enable gas-powered motors to operate.\n\nD) Enables windmills to power electric grids\nWindmills convert the kinetic energy of wind into electrical energy. This process is not directly related to decaying vegetation.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer.\nNone of the options provided are directly related to the process of decaying vegetation. However, if we consider the broader context of energy production and the environment, decaying vegetation contributes to the formation of fossil fuels over millions of years. Therefore, the closest answer would be:\n\nC) Enables gas-powered motors to operate",
                        "answers": [
