                    {
                        "id": "beed5951-1b31-4214-b98d-ac2a690fb32e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The original question is asking about an instance where light from a further away source appears to be less bright than a closer source. \n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. The brightness of a light source depends on its distance from the observer and its intrinsic brightness (luminosity).\n2. The sun is a star that is much closer to Earth than other stars.\n3. The moon is closer to Earth than the sun and other stars.\n4. A floodlight is a man-made light source that is typically much closer to the observer than celestial objects like the moon, sun, or stars.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Is the sun always bright?\n2. Is the moon brighter than stars?\n3. Is the moon brighter than a floodlight?\n4. Is the sun darker than the moon?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1. The sun is always bright due to its proximity to Earth and its high luminosity.\n2. The moon appears brighter than stars because it is much closer to Earth, even though its intrinsic brightness is lower than many stars.\n3. The moon may appear brighter or dimmer than a floodlight depending on the distance and brightness of the floodlight. However, in general, a floodlight is much closer to the observer than the moon, so it may appear brighter.\n4. The sun is not darker than the moon; it is much brighter due to its high luminosity and relatively close distance to Earth.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nLight from further away may appear to be less bright than other, closer sources, such as in the instance where the moon is brighter than stars (option B). This is because the moon is closer to Earth than stars, making it appear brighter even though its intrinsic brightness is lower than many stars.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4a3af4b3-d490-4b94-9bfa-044f9928ca6a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
