                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nTo answer this question, we need to think about how light works. Light is a type of energy that travels through the air and is used to see things. The brightness of light depends on how much energy is in the light. The more energy, the brighter the light.\n\nSo, when we say that light from further away may appear to be less bright, we are saying that the light has less energy. This can happen for a few reasons. One reason is that the light has to travel further to reach us, so some of the energy is lost along the way. Another reason is that the light may be coming from a weaker source, such as a star that is not as bright as the sun.\n\nSo, in answer to the question, the correct answer is D) the sun is darker than the moon.",
