                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) the moon is brighter than stars.\n\nTo work this out, we need to consider the distance of the light sources from the observer. The sun is the closest light source, and is always bright. The moon is further away than the sun, but closer than stars. Therefore, the moon will appear brighter than stars, which are further away. The moon may appear brighter than a floodlight, depending on the distance of the floodlight from the observer. The sun is never darker than the moon, since the sun is always the closest light source.",
