                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) the moon is brighter than stars\n\nComplementary Knowledge: The brightness of a light source is determined by its luminosity, which is the amount of energy it emits per unit of time. The further away a light source is, the less bright it appears to be.\n\nSub-Questions:\n1. How does the luminosity of the sun compare to the luminosity of the moon?\n2. How does the luminosity of the moon compare to the luminosity of stars?\n\nAnswer to Sub-Question 1: The sun has a much higher luminosity than the moon.\n\nAnswer to Sub-Question 2: The moon has a higher luminosity than stars.\n\nAnswer to Original Question: B) the moon is brighter than stars",
