                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define cellular respiration\n2. Identify the purpose of cellular respiration\n3. Determine the options provided in the question\n4. Eliminate the options that do not match the purpose of cellular respiration\n5. Choose the option that matches the purpose of cellular respiration\n\nAnswer: D) release energy\n\nExplanation:\n1. Cellular respiration is the process by which cells convert glucose and oxygen into energy, carbon dioxide, and water.\n2. The purpose of cellular respiration is to produce energy for the cell to carry out its functions.\n3. The options provided in the question are A) photosynthesize, B) release waste, C) perform meiosis, and D) release energy.\n4. Option A is incorrect because photosynthesis is the process by which plants produce glucose and oxygen using sunlight. Option B is incorrect because the release of waste is not the purpose of cellular respiration. Option C is incorrect because meiosis is the process by which cells divide to produce gametes for sexual reproduction. \n5. Therefore, the correct answer is D) release energy, which matches the purpose of cellular respiration.",
