                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm having trouble understanding this question about cellular respiration. Can you help me work through it?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's look at the question together. It says, \"All cells use cellular respiration to...\" and then gives us four options. Do you know what cellular respiration is?\n\nStudent: I think it's the process by which cells break down glucose to release energy, right?\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Now, let's look at the options and see which one matches that definition. Option A is \"photosynthesize.\" Do you think that's the right answer?\n\nStudent: No, I think photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert sunlight into energy.\n\nProfessor: Correct! So we can eliminate option A. Now, let's look at option B, \"release waste.\" What do you think about that one?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. I know cells release waste, but I don't know if that's the main purpose of cellular respiration.\n\nProfessor: You're right that cells do release waste, but that's not the primary function of cellular respiration. Cellular respiration is mainly about breaking down glucose to release energy, as you mentioned earlier. So, we can eliminate option B as well. Now, let's consider option C, \"perform meiosis.\" What are your thoughts on that?\n\nStudent: I think meiosis is a type of cell division, so I don't think that's the right answer either.\n\nProfessor: You're correct! Meiosis is a type of cell division that produces sex cells, so it's not related to cellular respiration. We can eliminate option C. That leaves us with option D, \"release energy.\" Based on our discussion, do you think that's the correct answer?\n\nStudent: Yes, I think that's the right answer because cellular respiration is all about breaking down glucose to release energy.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! So the correct answer is D, \"release energy.\" Great job working through the question step by step! Do you have any other questions about cellular respiration?\n\nStudent: No, I think I understand it now. Thank you for your help!",
