                    {
                        "id": "3f0ede43-b0c0-4e68-a1e5-4097b7245a57",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: Which of the following options best describes a desert environment?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\nA desert environment is characterized by its lack of precipitation, extreme temperatures, and sparse vegetation. Let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Dry, grass covered, and humid: This option is partially correct, as deserts are dry. However, they are not typically grass-covered or humid.\n\nB) Lush, green, and tropical: This option does not describe a desert environment, as these characteristics are more typical of a rainforest or tropical environment.\n\nC) Arid, parched, and sun-baked: This option accurately describes a desert environment, as it is dry (arid), has little moisture (parched), and receives a lot of sunlight (sun-baked).\n\nD) Dry, damp, and lush: This option is contradictory, as it is not possible for an environment to be both dry and damp at the same time. Additionally, deserts are not lush.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Arid, parched, and sun-baked.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e0e2c561-b7f8-41e5-9604-7a1406481c4a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
