                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify what an allergic reaction is.\n2. Understand the common symptoms of an allergic reaction.\n3. Determine the possible causes of an allergic reaction.\n4. Eliminate the options that are not related to allergic reactions.\n5. Choose the correct answer.\n\nAnswer: B) vomiting\n\nExplanation:\n1. An allergic reaction is a response of the immune system to a foreign substance that is not typically harmful to the body.\n2. Common symptoms of an allergic reaction include hives, itching, swelling, difficulty breathing, and vomiting.\n3. Possible causes of an allergic reaction include food, medication, insect bites, and environmental factors.\n4. Option A) spider bites, option C) placebo effect, and option D) dance fever are not related to allergic reactions.\n5. Therefore, the correct answer is B) vomiting, which is a common symptom of an allergic reaction.",
