                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) vomiting.\n\nMedicine is used to cure various illnesses and diseases. However, some people may have allergic reactions to certain medications. These allergic reactions can manifest in different ways, such as skin rashes, difficulty breathing, or vomiting.\n\nOption A) spider bites is not a correct answer as spider bites are not related to medicine or allergic reactions caused by medicine.\n\nOption C) placebo effect is not a correct answer as it is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. Placebo effect is a psychological phenomenon where a person experiences a perceived improvement in their condition after receiving a treatment that has no active ingredients.\n\nOption D) dance fever is not a correct answer as it is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. Dance fever is a term used to describe a phenomenon where people start dancing uncontrollably in large groups, often attributed to mass hysteria or psychological factors.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) vomiting, as it is a common symptom of an allergic reaction to medicine.",
