                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to identify which of the given options is an allergic reaction that can be caused by medicine.\n\nA) Spider bites - This is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. Spider bites are caused by spiders and are not related to medicine usage.\n\nB) Vomiting - This can be an allergic reaction caused by medicine. Some people may have an adverse reaction to certain medications, resulting in vomiting.\n\nC) Placebo effect - This is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. The placebo effect is a psychological phenomenon where a person experiences an improvement in their condition due to the belief that they are receiving treatment, even if the treatment is inactive or a \"dummy\" treatment.\n\nD) Dance fever - This is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. Dance fever is a colloquial term for a strong desire to dance, and it is not related to medicine usage.\n\nBased on the analysis above, the correct answer is:\n\nB) Vomiting",
