                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following is a possible allergic reaction to medicine?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nA) Spider bites - This is not an allergic reaction to medicine. Spider bites are caused by spiders, not medicine.\n\nB) Vomiting - This could be a possible allergic reaction to medicine. Some people may experience vomiting as a side effect or allergic reaction to certain medications.\n\nC) Placebo effect - This is not an allergic reaction to medicine. The placebo effect is a psychological phenomenon where a person experiences an improvement in their condition after receiving a treatment with no active ingredients, simply because they believe the treatment will work.\n\nD) Dance fever - This is not an allergic reaction to medicine. Dance fever is a colloquial term for a strong desire to dance, and it is not related to medicine or allergies.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nB) Vomiting",
