                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Medicine is used to cure but can cause people to have allergic reactions such as A) spider bites B) vomiting C) placebo effect D) dance fever\n\nAdditional Facts:\n- Allergic reactions are the body's immune system responding to a foreign substance.\n- Common symptoms of allergic reactions include itching, swelling, hives, and difficulty breathing.\n- Medicines can cause side effects, which are unintended and sometimes harmful effects of the drug.\n- Allergic reactions to medicines are a type of side effect.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) What are the common symptoms of allergic reactions to medicines?\n2) Which of the given options are symptoms of allergic reactions or side effects of medicines?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1) Common symptoms of allergic reactions to medicines include itching, swelling, hives, difficulty breathing, and in severe cases, anaphylaxis.\n2) \nA) Spider bites - Not a symptom of an allergic reaction to medicine. It is an external factor that can cause an allergic reaction itself.\nB) Vomiting - Can be a symptom of an allergic reaction or a side effect of medicine.\nC) Placebo effect - Not a symptom of an allergic reaction. It is a psychological phenomenon where a person experiences an improvement in their condition due to the belief that they are receiving treatment.\nD) Dance fever - Not a symptom of an allergic reaction or a side effect of medicine. It is a colloquial term and not related to medical conditions or treatments.\n\nAnswer to the original question: Medicine is used to cure but can cause people to have allergic reactions such as B) vomiting.",
                        "answers": [
