                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) vomiting.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to consider the definition of medicine and the definition of an allergic reaction. Medicine is defined as a substance used to treat, cure, or prevent a disease or illness. An allergic reaction is defined as an exaggerated response of the immune system to a substance that is generally not harmful.\n\nBased on these definitions, we can eliminate A) spider bites and D) dance fever as they are not related to medicine or an allergic reaction.\n\nNext, we need to consider C) placebo effect. A placebo effect is a phenomenon in which a patient's symptoms are alleviated by a treatment that has no active therapeutic effect. This is not an allergic reaction, so we can eliminate C) placebo effect as well.\n\nThis leaves us with B) vomiting as the correct answer. Vomiting is a common symptom of an allergic reaction, and it can be treated with medicine.",
