                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how electricity can be made from moving winds?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Electricity can be generated from moving winds through the use of wind turbines. Wind turbines are large structures with blades that rotate when the wind blows. The rotation of the blades turns a generator, which produces electricity.\n\nStudent: How much electricity can be generated from wind turbines?\n\nProfessor: The amount of electricity generated depends on the size of the wind turbine and the strength of the wind. Generally, larger wind turbines can generate more electricity than smaller ones. A single wind turbine can generate enough electricity to power several homes.\n\nStudent: Are there any downsides to using wind turbines to generate electricity?\n\nProfessor: One downside is that wind turbines can be noisy and can cause visual pollution. They also require a lot of space and can be expensive to install. Additionally, wind turbines are not always reliable sources of electricity because they depend on the wind, which can be unpredictable.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that to me.",
