                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The helpful knowledge and important additional facts are that Earth is a planet in our solar system and is the third planet from the sun. It has a solid surface and a molten core, and it is the only known planet to support life.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is Earth made of?\n2. What is the structure of Earth's interior?\n3. How does Earth's structure contribute to its sturdiness?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Earth is made of rock and metal. The outermost layer, the crust, is made of solid rock. The mantle is made of solid and molten rock, and the core is made of molten metal.\n2. Earth's interior is divided into three layers: the crust, the mantle, and the core. The crust is the thinnest layer and is made of solid rock. The mantle is thicker and is made of solid and molten rock. The core is the innermost layer and is made of molten metal.\n3. Earth's sturdiness is due to its solid surface and its molten core. The solid surface provides a stable foundation for life to thrive, while the molten core generates a magnetic field that protects the planet from harmful solar radiation and cosmic rays. Additionally, the movement of the molten rock in the mantle creates tectonic plates that help to regulate the planet's temperature and maintain its stability.",
