                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the correct answer, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) It is made from rock: Earth is indeed composed of various types of rocks, minerals, and other materials. The solid surface of the Earth, known as the crust, is primarily made up of rocks. This could be a possible reason for Earth's sturdiness.\n\nB) It eats three meals a day: This statement is not applicable to Earth, as it is a planet and not a living organism. It does not eat meals. Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\nC) It has a loving family: This statement is also not applicable to Earth, as it is a planet and not a living organism. It does not have a family. Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\nD) It is made from metal: While Earth does contain some metal elements, such as iron and nickel, it is not primarily made from metal. The Earth's core is composed of a mixture of metals, but the overall composition of the Earth is not predominantly metal. Therefore, this option is not the best answer.\n\nBased on the analysis of each option, the correct answer is:\n\nA) It is made from rock. Earth's sturdiness can be attributed to its composition, which includes various types of rocks, minerals, and other materials.",
