                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking for the reason why Earth is sturdy. To answer this question, we need to understand the composition of Earth and what makes it sturdy.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. Earth is composed of various layers, including the crust, mantle, outer core, and inner core.\n2. The crust and mantle are primarily made of rock, while the outer core is composed of molten metal, and the inner core is solid metal.\n3. The sturdiness of Earth is due to the strength and stability of its composition and structure.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the properties of rock that contribute to Earth's sturdiness?\n2. What are the properties of metal that contribute to Earth's sturdiness?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1. Rock is a solid, naturally occurring substance that is composed of minerals. It is strong, durable, and resistant to erosion and weathering, which contributes to Earth's sturdiness.\n2. Metal is a material that is typically hard, shiny, malleable, fusible, and ductile, with good electrical and thermal conductivity. The presence of metal in Earth's core provides strength and stability to the planet's structure, contributing to its sturdiness.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nThe reason Earth is so sturdy is because A) It is made from rock and D) It is made from metal. Both rock and metal contribute to the strength and stability of Earth's composition and structure.",
