                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how genetics contribute to a rabbit having long ears?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Genetics is the study of how traits are passed down from parents to offspring. In the case of rabbits, the genes that control ear length are passed down from the parents to their offspring.\n\nStudent: So, if both parents have long ears, their offspring will also have long ears?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. If both parents have the genes for long ears, then their offspring will inherit those genes and have long ears as well.\n\nStudent: What if only one parent has long ears?\n\nProfessor: In that case, it depends on whether the gene for long ears is dominant or recessive. If the gene is dominant, then the offspring will have long ears even if only one parent has the gene. If the gene is recessive, then the offspring will only have long ears if both parents have the gene.\n\nStudent: How do we know which genes are dominant and which are recessive?\n\nProfessor: That's determined through genetic testing and analysis. Scientists have identified which genes are responsible for certain traits, and they've also determined whether those genes are dominant or recessive. It's a complex process, but it's how we understand the genetics of different organisms, including rabbits.",
