                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define what is meant by \"resources\" in this context.\n2. Consider how organisms typically respond to a decrease in resources.\n3. Evaluate each answer choice in light of this information.\n\nAnswer: D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources.\n\nExplanation:\n1. Resources in this context likely refer to things like food, water, and shelter that are necessary for an organism's survival.\n2. When resources become scarce, organisms typically adjust their behavior to conserve what resources they do have. This might mean reducing activity levels, seeking out new sources of resources, or becoming more efficient in their use of resources.\n3. Answer choice A is incorrect because it suggests that organisms would use more resources when they are becoming scarce, which is counterintuitive. Answer choice B is also incorrect for the same reason. Answer choice C is unlikely because an increase in birthrate would only exacerbate the problem of resource scarcity. Answer choice D is the most likely answer because it aligns with what we know about how organisms typically respond to resource scarcity.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "5c451cc7-d403-468c-97a7-5231a2fe99c7",
