                    {
                        "id": "34d63ca3-8316-4a9f-b3de-7a4728fdb9f3",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources.\n\nWhen resources in an environment decrease, organisms are faced with a scarcity of resources. In order to survive, they must adapt to this scarcity by being more efficient with the resources they have. This means that they will use less of their resources and be more economical with them. This is because they need to conserve their resources in order to survive until more resources become available. Therefore, option D is the correct answer.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "acf91fe7-be45-40a0-a459-2a8de5847282",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
