                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking about the effect of decreasing resources in an environment on the organisms living in that environment.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nA) induces organisms to use more of their resources: This option suggests that organisms will use more resources when there are fewer resources available. This doesn't make sense, as organisms would likely try to conserve resources when they are scarce.\n\nB) causes an increase in use of resources: This option is similar to option A and also doesn't make sense, as organisms would likely try to conserve resources when they are scarce.\n\nC) causes an uptick in birthrate: This option suggests that a decrease in resources would lead to an increase in birthrate. This is unlikely, as organisms would generally reproduce less when resources are scarce to ensure the survival of existing individuals.\n\nD) induces organisms to be more economical with resources: This option suggests that organisms will try to use resources more efficiently when resources are scarce. This makes sense, as organisms would need to adapt to the limited resources to survive.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources.",
