                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking how organisms respond when resources in their environment decrease.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the answer choices\nA) induces organisms to use more of their resources\nB) causes an increase in use of resources\nC) causes an uptick in birthrate\nD) induces organisms to be more economical with resources\n\nStep 3: Evaluate each answer choice\nA) This choice suggests that organisms will use more resources when there are fewer resources available. This does not make sense, as organisms would likely try to conserve resources when they are scarce.\nB) Similar to choice A, this choice suggests that organisms will increase their use of resources when there are fewer resources available. This also does not make sense for the same reasons.\nC) This choice suggests that organisms will have a higher birthrate when resources are scarce. This is unlikely, as organisms would likely struggle to support more offspring when resources are limited.\nD) This choice suggests that organisms will be more economical with resources when there are fewer resources available. This makes sense, as organisms would likely try to conserve resources when they are scarce.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best answer\nBased on the analysis, the best answer is D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources.",
