                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Muscles are made up of muscle tissue, which is responsible for movement and contraction in the body. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is muscle tissue?\nMuscle tissue is a type of tissue in the body that is responsible for movement and contraction. \n\n2. Which organs in the body contain muscle tissue?\nOrgans that contain muscle tissue include the heart, skeletal muscles, smooth muscles in the digestive system, and the uterus. \n\n3. Which of the organs listed (lungs, kidney, heart, liver) contain muscle tissue?\nThe lungs and kidneys do not contain muscle tissue. The heart contains cardiac muscle tissue, which is responsible for pumping blood throughout the body. The liver does not contain muscle tissue. \n\nAnswer:\nThe most muscular organ out of the options given is the heart, as it contains cardiac muscle tissue.",
