                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm trying to figure out which organ is the most muscular. Can you help me out?\n\nProfessor: Sure, which organs are you considering?\n\nStudent: I'm considering the lungs, kidney, heart, and liver.\n\nProfessor: Okay, well let's start by eliminating the lungs and kidney. While they do have some muscle tissue, it's not enough to make them the most muscular organ.\n\nStudent: Okay, so that leaves the heart and liver. Which one is more muscular?\n\nProfessor: The heart is actually the most muscular organ in the body. It's made up of thick, strong muscle tissue that contracts and relaxes to pump blood throughout the body.\n\nStudent: That's interesting. How does the liver compare in terms of muscle?\n\nProfessor: The liver does have some muscle tissue, but it's not nearly as much as the heart. The liver's main function is to filter blood and produce bile, so it doesn't need as much muscle as the heart does.\n\nStudent: I see. So, just to clarify, the heart is the most muscular organ because it has the most muscle tissue and needs it to pump blood throughout the body?\n\nProfessor: Exactly. The heart is a very important organ that needs a lot of muscle to do its job effectively.",
