                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which organ among the given options is the most muscular.\n\nStep 2: Define muscular\nAn organ being muscular means it is primarily composed of muscle tissue, which is responsible for producing force and motion.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the options\nA) The lungs - The lungs are responsible for respiration and gas exchange. They are not primarily composed of muscle tissue.\nB) The kidney - The kidneys are responsible for filtering blood and producing urine. They are not primarily composed of muscle tissue.\nC) The heart - The heart is responsible for pumping blood throughout the body. It is primarily composed of cardiac muscle tissue.\nD) The liver - The liver is responsible for detoxification, protein synthesis, and production of bile. It is not primarily composed of muscle tissue.\n\nStep 4: Choose the most muscular organ\nBased on the analysis of the options, the heart (C) is the most muscular organ among the given choices.",
