                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking us to determine which of the given organs is the most muscular. \n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nA) The lungs: The lungs are responsible for respiration and gas exchange. They are made up of soft, spongy tissue and are not considered muscular.\nB) The kidney: The kidneys are responsible for filtering waste products from the blood and maintaining electrolyte balance. They are made up of nephrons and are not considered muscular.\nC) The heart: The heart is responsible for pumping blood throughout the body. It is made up of cardiac muscle, which is a type of muscle tissue that is specifically designed for continuous contraction and relaxation. The heart is considered a muscular organ.\nD) The liver: The liver is responsible for detoxification, protein synthesis, and production of bile. It is made up of hepatocytes and is not considered muscular.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most muscular organ\nBased on the analysis of the options, the heart (option C) is the most muscular organ among the given choices.",
