                    {
                        "id": "2984f570-e491-431d-9fae-a38151de9633",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the functions of each organ and their composition. The main function of each organ is as follows:\n\nA) Lungs: Responsible for gas exchange, allowing oxygen to enter the bloodstream and carbon dioxide to be expelled.\nB) Kidney: Filters waste products and excess substances from the blood, maintaining proper electrolyte balance and producing urine.\nC) Heart: Pumps blood throughout the body, supplying oxygen and nutrients to tissues and removing waste products.\nD) Liver: Processes nutrients absorbed from the digestive system, detoxifies harmful substances, and produces bile for digestion.\n\nNow, let's consider the composition of each organ:\n\nA) Lungs: Primarily composed of soft, spongy tissue with some smooth muscle to help with expansion and contraction during breathing.\nB) Kidney: Primarily composed of nephrons (functional units for filtration) and some smooth muscle to help with urine production.\nC) Heart: Primarily composed of cardiac muscle, which is responsible for the continuous contraction and relaxation needed to pump blood.\nD) Liver: Primarily composed of hepatocytes (liver cells) and some smooth muscle to help with bile production.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Which organ has the highest proportion of muscle tissue?\nAnswer: The heart, as it is primarily composed of cardiac muscle.\n\n2) How do the other organs compare in terms of muscle content?\nAnswer: The lungs, kidney, and liver all have some smooth muscle, but their primary functions are carried out by other types of cells and tissues.\n\nBased on the information above, the most muscular organ among the options is:\n\nC) the heart",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0b077f5c-6492-4e1e-9097-4a4032edfec9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) the heart, as it is primarily composed of cardiac muscle and its main function requires continuous contraction and relaxation to pump blood throughout the body. The other organs, while containing some smooth muscle, rely more on other types of cells and tissues for their primary functions.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
