                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nTo determine which organ is the most muscular, we need to consider the function of each organ and how it relates to muscle. \n\nThe lungs are responsible for respiration, which involves the contraction and relaxation of muscles in the chest and abdomen to draw air in and out of the lungs. Therefore, the lungs are not the most muscular organ. \n\nThe kidneys are responsible for filtering waste from the blood and regulating the body's water balance. The kidneys do not involve any muscle contraction, so they are not the most muscular organ. \n\nThe heart is responsible for pumping blood throughout the body. The heart is composed of cardiac muscle, which is a type of involuntary muscle that contracts and relaxes to pump blood. Therefore, the heart is the most muscular organ. \n\nThe liver is responsible for filtering toxins from the blood and producing bile. The liver does not involve any muscle contraction, so it is not the most muscular organ. \n\nTherefore, the answer is C) the heart.",
