                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is D) music.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we can consider the definitions of each of the words in the choices.\n\nA) planets: A planet is a celestial body that orbits a star, has sufficient mass for its gravity to overcome rigid body forces so that it assumes a hydrostatic equilibrium shape, and has cleared its neighbouring region of planetesimals. Planets do not travel through the air.\n\nB) thoughts: Thoughts are ideas, opinions, or images that occur in the mind. Thoughts do not travel through the air.\n\nC) automobile: An automobile is a wheeled vehicle that carries its own motor and transports passengers. Automobiles do not travel through the air.\n\nD) music: Music is an art form and cultural activity whose medium is sound organized in time. Music can travel through the air, as sound waves are transmitted through the air.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) music.",
