                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding how to determine the correct answer for this question about how frogs can get warm. Can you help me work through it?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option one by one and see if it makes sense for a frog. First, can a frog wear a Christmas sweater?\n\nStudent: Well, I guess not, since they don't have arms or the ability to put on clothes.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. So we can eliminate option A. Now, what about drinking hot chocolate?\n\nStudent: I don't think frogs can drink hot chocolate because they don't have the ability to hold a cup, and I'm not sure if it's safe for them to consume.\n\nProfessor: You're right again. Frogs don't have the ability to hold a cup, and hot chocolate could be harmful to them. So we can eliminate option B. Moving on to option C, can a frog go for a run?\n\nStudent: I think frogs can move around, but I'm not sure if that would help them get warm.\n\nProfessor: Good observation. While frogs can move around, they are ectothermic, which means they rely on external sources to regulate their body temperature. So, going for a run wouldn't help them get warm. That leaves us with option D, sitting under a lamp. What do you think about that?\n\nStudent: That seems like it could work, since the lamp would provide heat and help the frog get warm.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! Frogs can sit under a lamp to get warm because the heat from the lamp will help regulate their body temperature. So the correct answer is option D.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor! I understand how we got to the right answer now.",
