                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the term used to describe the process of worms returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil by eating them?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Regurgitation refers to the process of bringing up partially digested food from the stomach to the mouth, which is not what worms do with dead organisms.\n- Burial refers to the act of putting something underground, which is not what worms do with dead organisms either.\n- Decomposition is the process of breaking down organic matter into simpler substances, which is related to what worms do with dead organisms, but it doesn't capture the fact that they are returning nutrients to the soil.\n- Recycling is the process of converting waste into reusable material, which seems to fit the description of what worms do with dead organisms.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) recycling. \n\nFinal answer: The term used to describe the process of worms returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil by eating them is recycling.",
