                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\n1. Read the question carefully: The question is asking for the term used to describe the process of worms returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil by eating them.\n\n2. Identify the options: The options are regurgitation, decomposition, recycling, and burial.\n\n3. Eliminate incorrect options: Regurgitation and burial are not correct because they do not accurately describe the process of worms returning nutrients to the soil. \n\n4. Choose the best answer: The correct answer is C) recycling, as it accurately describes the process of worms returning nutrients to the soil by eating dead organisms.\n\n5. Check the answer: Recycling is the process of converting waste into reusable material. In this case, worms are converting dead organisms into nutrients that can be reused by other organisms in the soil. Therefore, recycling is the correct answer.",
