                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the process being described - worms eating dead organisms and returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each option and determine which one best fits the process.\n\nA) Regurgitation - This refers to the process of expelling swallowed food back up through the mouth. This does not fit the process being described.\n\nB) Decomposition - This is the process of breaking down dead organic material into simpler compounds, which can be returned to the soil. This is a part of the process being described, but it does not specifically mention the role of worms.\n\nC) Recycling - This refers to the process of converting waste materials into new products or reusing them in some way. In this context, worms are recycling nutrients from dead organisms back into the soil, so this is a possible answer.\n\nD) Burial - This refers to the act of placing something in the ground, typically as a means of disposal. While worms may bury dead organisms, this does not specifically describe the process of returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nStep 3: Choose the best answer based on the analysis.\n\nThe best answer is C) recycling, as it specifically describes the process of worms returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil by eating them.",
