                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question - The question is asking what the process is called when worms consume dead organisms and return nutrients to the soil.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the answer choices - We have four options: regurgitation, decomposition, recycling, and burial.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate each answer choice:\n\nA) Regurgitation - This refers to the process of expelling swallowed food back up through the mouth. This does not describe the process of worms returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nB) Decomposition - This is the process of breaking down organic matter into simpler compounds. While worms do contribute to decomposition, the question specifically asks about the process of worms consuming dead organisms and returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nC) Recycling - This term generally refers to the process of converting waste materials into new products or reusing materials. In the context of worms and nutrients, this could be a possible answer.\n\nD) Burial - This refers to the act of placing something in the ground, typically as a means of disposal. This does not describe the process of worms consuming dead organisms and returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best answer - Based on the evaluation of each answer choice, the best answer is C) recycling, as it describes the process of worms consuming dead organisms and returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nAnswer: C) recycling",
