                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand the process that is being described.\n\nWhen worms eat dead organisms, they break down the organic matter and release nutrients back into the soil. This process is essential for maintaining soil fertility and promoting plant growth.\n\nNow, let's analyze each of the given options:\n\nA) Regurgitation: This term refers to the process of expelling swallowed food back up through the mouth. This is not the process being described in the question.\n\nB) Decomposition: This term refers to the process of breaking down organic matter into simpler compounds. While decomposition is a part of the process being described, it does not specifically refer to the action of worms returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nC) Recycling: This term refers to the process of converting waste materials into new products or reusing them in some way. In the context of the question, worms are essentially recycling nutrients from dead organisms back into the soil, making this a suitable answer.\n\nD) Burial: This term refers to the act of placing something in the ground, typically as a means of disposal. While worms do burrow through the soil, this term does not accurately describe the process of returning nutrients to the soil.\n\nBased on the analysis of each option, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Recycling",
                        "answers": [
