                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: What is the process called when worms consume dead organisms and release nutrients back into the soil?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step, spelling out our thoughts and reasoning:\n\nA) Regurgitation: This refers to the process of expelling swallowed food back up through the mouth. This doesn't seem to fit the description of the process we're looking for.\n\nB) Decomposition: This is the process of breaking down organic matter into simpler compounds, which can be carried out by various organisms, including worms. This seems like a possible answer.\n\nC) Recycling: This term generally refers to the process of converting waste materials into new products, but it doesn't specifically describe the process of worms consuming dead organisms and releasing nutrients back into the soil.\n\nD) Burial: This refers to the act of placing something in the ground, such as a dead body. While worms may help in the decomposition process by burrowing through the soil, this term doesn't accurately describe the process we're looking for.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is B) Decomposition, as it best describes the process of worms consuming dead organisms and releasing nutrients back into the soil.",
