                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of each of the answer choices.\n\nA) Regurgitation: the act of bringing up food that has been swallowed and partially digested.\n\nB) Decomposition: the process by which organic substances are broken down into simpler forms of matter.\n\nC) Recycling: the process of converting waste materials into new products.\n\nD) Burial: the act of placing something in the ground.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the question and determine which answer choice best fits the definition.\n\nThe question states that worms are returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil by eating them. This process does not involve placing something in the ground, so answer choice D (burial) is not the correct answer. The process does involve breaking down organic substances into simpler forms of matter, so answer choice B (decomposition) is the correct answer.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "43e74c87-b379-4fc3-96ea-51b5cd08f2b3",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
