                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) sandstorms create ripples in sand.\n\nTo see how wind affects sand, we need to observe the movement of sand particles caused by wind. Option A states that sand is always moving, but this does not necessarily mean that it is due to wind. Option C states that sand is easy to move through, but this does not provide any information on how wind affects sand. Option D mentions waves in the sand, but this could be caused by water and not wind.\n\nOption B, on the other hand, specifically mentions sandstorms, which are caused by strong winds blowing sand particles across the ground. Sandstorms create ripples in the sand, which are visible evidence of the wind's effect on the sand. Therefore, option B is the correct answer.",
