                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What are the ways in which we can observe the impact of wind on sand?\n\nFirst, let's consider each option and evaluate its relevance to the question.\n\nA) Sand is always moving: This statement is true, but it does not specifically address how wind affects sand. Sand can move due to various factors, such as water currents or human activity.\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand: This option directly relates to the impact of wind on sand. Sandstorms, which are caused by strong winds, can create ripples and other patterns in the sand as they move and displace the sand particles.\n\nC) Sand is easy to move through: This statement is true, but it does not specifically address how wind affects sand. The ease of movement through sand is more related to its physical properties rather than the impact of wind.\n\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand: This option also relates to the impact of wind on sand. Wind can create waves and ripples in the sand on beaches, as it moves and displaces the sand particles.\n\nAfter evaluating each option, we can conclude that the ways in which we can observe the impact of wind on sand are:\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f0bbd3ce-9b23-4d04-a867-eec2292f99b2",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B and D.",
                                "answer_from_choices": null,
                                "correct_answer": null
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 03:35:25",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-4', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "48ad0151-c239-4ba4-8293-5102ddbf1971",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To see how wind affects sand, we need to consider the properties of sand and the ways in which wind interacts with it. Sand is a granular material composed of small particles, which makes it susceptible to movement by external forces such as wind. Wind can cause sand to move in various ways, such as creating ripples, dunes, or even sandstorms.\n\nSome important additional facts to consider are:\n- The strength and direction of the wind can influence the movement of sand.\n- The size and weight of sand particles can also affect how easily they are moved by wind.\n- The presence of moisture in the sand can impact its movement, as wet sand tends to stick together and is less easily moved by wind.\n\nTo answer the original question, we can generate the following sub-questions:\n1. How does wind create ripples in sand?\n2. How does wind create sand dunes?\n3. How does wind cause sandstorms?\n\n1. Wind creates ripples in sand by blowing sand particles across the surface. As the wind moves the sand, it forms small ridges and troughs, creating a rippled pattern. This can be observed on beaches and in deserts, where wind is a primary force shaping the landscape.\n\n2. Wind creates sand dunes by moving sand particles over time and depositing them in specific areas. As the wind blows, it carries sand particles and deposits them when the wind speed decreases or encounters an obstacle. Over time, these deposits accumulate and form sand dunes. The shape and size of the dunes depend on factors such as wind speed, direction, and the availability of sand.\n\n3. Wind causes sandstorms when it is strong enough to lift large amounts of sand particles into the air. These particles can then be carried by the wind over long distances, creating a sandstorm. Sandstorms can cause reduced visibility, damage to structures, and even health issues for people and animals exposed to the airborne sand.\n\nIn conclusion, we can see how wind affects sand through the creation of ripples, sand dunes, and sandstorms. These phenomena demonstrate the power of wind to shape and move sand in various ways, which can be observed in natural environments such as beaches and deserts.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "955a179e-f090-4a5d-bebc-6e865a704810",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) sandstorms create ripples in sand and D) beaches often have waves in the sand.",
                                "answer_from_choices": null,
                                "correct_answer": null
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 03:36:26",
