                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nTo see how wind affects sand, we can observe the following: \n\nA) Sand is always moving - Wind can cause sand to move in different directions, creating patterns in the sand. We can observe this by looking at the sand and seeing which direction it is moving in.\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand - When a sandstorm occurs, the wind can cause the sand to form ripples in the sand. We can observe this by looking at the sand and seeing the ripples that have been created.\n\nC) Sand is easy to move through - Wind can cause sand to move easily through the air. We can observe this by looking at the sand and seeing how easily it moves when the wind blows.\n\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand - Wind can cause waves to form in the sand on beaches. We can observe this by looking at the sand on the beach and seeing the waves that have been created.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4044849c-2aca-44da-9be1-64bd0b69a7af",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
