                        "cot": "\n\nTo calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's mother, you would need to know the genotypes of both the mother and the father. If both the mother and father are heterozygous for the trait, then the chance of the trait being passed to the child is 50%. If the mother is homozygous for the trait and the father is heterozygous, then the chance of the trait being passed to the child is 100%. If the mother is heterozygous and the father is homozygous for the trait, then the chance of the trait being passed to the child is also 100%.",
