                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA Punnett square can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's offspring. The mother and father each contribute one allele to their child, and the alleles can be the same or different. If the alleles are the same, then the child will have the same trait as the parent. If the alleles are different, then the child will have a mixture of the two traits.",
