                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Can you help me understand how to use a Punnett square?\n\nProfessor: Sure. A Punnett square is a way to calculate the chance of a trait being passed on to someone's offspring.\n\nStudent: So how would I use it to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to my daughter?\n\nProfessor: You would need to know the genotypes of both you and your partner. Let's say your genotype is AA and your partner's genotype is BB. You would then create a Punnett square with the A and B alleles on the top and sides.\n\n\n\nA\nA\nA\nA\n\nB\nB\nB\nB\n\nStudent: So in this example, each child would have a 25% chance of having the trait?\n\nProfessor: That's right.",
