                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the basic principles of sailing and how a sailor can navigate a boat towards the shore. \n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. Sailing is the art of controlling a boat with large fabric sails that catch the wind.\n2. The rudder is a flat piece of wood, fiberglass, or metal that is used to steer a ship or boat.\n3. Adjusting the rudder changes the direction of the boat.\n4. Closing the sails quickly would slow down the boat, but not necessarily change its direction.\n5. Setting out to sea would mean moving away from the shore, not towards it.\n6. Taking the afternoon off would not help the sailor navigate towards the shore.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Which of the given options would help the sailor change the direction of the boat towards the shore?\n\nAnswer: Making an adjustment to the rudder (C) would help the sailor change the direction of the boat towards the shore.\n\n2. Are any of the other options helpful in navigating towards the shore?\n\nAnswer: No, the other options (A, B, and D) would not help the sailor navigate towards the shore.\n\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, the sailor needs to navigate to the shore by making an adjustment to the rudder (C).",
