                    {
                        "id": "8d000386-bec9-43ab-8de2-8fe1de3440ca",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand what characterizes a desert. A desert is a region with very low precipitation and little vegetation, often due to a lack of water. One of the main reasons for this lack of water is the high evaporation rate caused by the intense sunlight and heat.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) they get low sunlight - This statement is incorrect, as deserts are known for their high sunlight and heat.\n\nB) deserts get surplus sun - This statement is correct, as deserts receive a lot of sunlight, which contributes to their high evaporation rates and dry conditions.\n\nC) deserts get little sun - This statement is incorrect, as it contradicts the fact that deserts receive a lot of sunlight.\n\nD) deserts are always cloudy - This statement is incorrect, as deserts are known for their clear skies and lack of cloud cover, which allows for more sunlight to reach the ground.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nB) deserts get surplus sun",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0bac7cd9-953f-4902-974d-20f6736b51a2",
