                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of a desert.\n\nA desert is a dry, barren area of land that receives very little rainfall and has extreme temperatures.\n\nStep 2: Consider the options.\n\nA) they get low sunlight\nB) deserts get surplus sun\nC) deserts get little sun\nD) deserts are always cloudy\n\nStep 3: Eliminate options that are not true.\n\nA) they get low sunlight - False, deserts get very little sunlight.\nB) deserts get surplus sun - False, deserts get very little sunlight.\nD) deserts are always cloudy - False, deserts can be sunny.\n\nStep 4: Select the correct answer.\n\nC) deserts get little sun - True, deserts get very little sunlight.",
