                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Read the question carefully to understand what is being asked.\n\nThe question is asking about the characteristics of objects used to hold sheets of paper together.\n\nStep 2: Consider each answer option and eliminate any that are clearly incorrect.\n\nA) Large: This answer option does not make sense as paper clips, staples, and binder clips are all small objects used to hold sheets of paper together.\n\nB) Wooden: While it is possible to make paper clips or staples out of wood, it is not a common material used for these objects.\n\nC) Ferromagnetic: This answer option refers to materials that are attracted to magnets, such as iron or steel. While some paper clips and staples may be made of these materials, not all of them are.\n\nD) Electronic: This answer option does not make sense as paper clips, staples, and binder clips are all simple mechanical objects that do not require electronic components.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer.\n\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is C) ferromagnetic. While not all paper clips and staples are made of ferromagnetic materials, some are, and this is a characteristic that is commonly associated with these objects.",
