                    {
                        "id": "27d47c05-0e4c-4d76-bd2d-ba6b57919adf",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Running at night can be dangerous because it is harder for drivers to see pedestrians in the dark. Reflective gear can help increase visibility and reduce the risk of accidents.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a reflector?\n2. How does a reflector work?\n3. What materials are reflective?\n4. Which of the given options are reflective?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A reflector is a material or object that reflects light.\n2. When light hits a reflector, it bounces off in a different direction, making the object more visible.\n3. Materials that are reflective include reflective tape, reflective paint, and certain fabrics.\n4. A) A black shirt is not reflective. B) Kitchen foil can be reflective, but it is not a practical option for running as it is not durable or comfortable. C) Sunglasses are not reflective. D) A megaphone is not reflective. \n\nTherefore, the answer is none of the given options. Instead, one could use reflective tape, a reflective vest, or a headlamp with a reflective strap.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d2e40d7f-232a-4d62-817a-0181afc1b8d5",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
