                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: What is echolocation?\n\nProfessor: Echolocation is a way for animals to detect objects by using sound waves.\n\nStudent: What kind of animals use echolocation?\n\nProfessor: Bats and dolphins are two examples of animals that use echolocation.\n\nStudent: How does echolocation work?\n\nProfessor: Animals that use echolocation emit sound waves, and then they listen for the waves to bounce back. By interpreting the waves that bounce back, they can determine the location, distance, and size of an object.\n\nStudent: So echolocation can't detect an object's temperature?\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Echolocation can only detect an object's distance, shape, and size.",
