                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What is echolocation?\nEcholocation is a biological sonar system used by some animals, such as bats and dolphins, to navigate and locate prey or obstacles by emitting high-pitched sounds and listening for the echoes that bounce back.\n\nStep 2: What information can echolocation detect?\nEcholocation can detect an object's distance, shape, and size by analyzing the time delay and frequency of the echoes. This allows animals to create a mental map of their surroundings and avoid collisions.\n\nStep 3: What information can echolocation not detect?\nEcholocation cannot detect an object's temperature. This is because temperature does not affect the reflection of sound waves, which is what echolocation relies on.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) temperature.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3dcfe435-c6db-4f73-ad17-0f864aac19ac",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) temperature.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
