                        "cot": "\nThe most likely cause of the decreasing amount of brush in the park is A) the season has been quite dry. This is because dry conditions can cause plants to die off due to lack of water, leading to a decrease in the amount of brush in the park. Additionally, dry conditions can also cause an increase in the amount of fires, which can also lead to a decrease in the amount of brush in the park. \n\nB) There has been a lot of rain is not as likely a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in the park because rain is usually beneficial for plants, leading to an increase in the amount of brush in the park. \n\nC) snakes shelter under the brush is not as likely a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in the park because snakes do not typically cause plants to die off, and therefore would not lead to a decrease in the amount of brush in the park. \n\nD) People have been walking by the brush on the trails is not as likely a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in the park because people walking by the brush would not typically cause plants to die off, and therefore would not lead to a decrease in the amount of brush in the park.",
