                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question: What could be a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in a park?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step:\nA) the season has been quite dry - This could be a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in a park because dry conditions can cause plants to die or become dormant.\n\nB) There has been a lot of rain - This could be a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in a park because too much rain can cause plants to become waterlogged and die.\n\nC) snakes shelter under the brush - This could be a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in a park because if people are scared of snakes and avoid the area, the brush may not be getting enough sunlight or water to survive.\n\nD) People have been walking by the brush on the trails - This could be a cause of the decreasing amount of brush in a park because people walking on the trails can trample the brush and cause it to die.\n\nThird, let's make sure we have the right answer: All of the above could be causes of the decreasing amount of brush in a park.",
