                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe amount of brush in a park has been decreasing, which could be caused by a variety of factors. To answer this question, it is important to consider the environment of the park, the type of brush, and the activity of people in the park. \n\nSub-question 1: What is the environment of the park?\nA) Is the park in a dry climate?\nB) Is the park in a wet climate?\n\nSub-question 2: What type of brush is in the park?\nA) Is the brush native to the area?\nB) Is the brush non-native to the area?\n\nSub-question 3: What activity of people is in the park?\nA) Are people walking on the trails?\nB) Are people cutting down the brush?\n\nAnswer: The cause of the decreasing amount of brush in the park could be A) the season has been quite dry, B) There has been a lot of rain, C) snakes shelter under the brush, or D) People have been walking by the brush on the trails. The answer will depend on the environment of the park, the type of brush, and the activity of people in the park.",
