                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Identify the main components of photosynthesis.\n- Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose or other sugars. The main components involved in this process are carbon dioxide (CO2), water (H2O), and sunlight.\n\nStep 2: Compare the main components with the given options.\n- Option A: CO2, water, and argon. Argon is not involved in photosynthesis.\n- Option B: Sunlight, oxygen, and fertilizer. Oxygen is a product of photosynthesis, not a required ingredient, and fertilizer is not directly involved in the process.\n- Option C: CO2, H2O, and cloudy skies. Cloudy skies can reduce the amount of sunlight available for photosynthesis, but they are not a required ingredient.\n- Option D: CO2, H2O, and sun rays. This option includes all the main components of photosynthesis.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct option.\n- The correct option is D) CO2, H2O, and sun rays.",
