                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand what \"Fe\" represents in the context of a nail. \n\nFe is the chemical symbol for the element Iron. The atomic number of Iron is 26, which means it has 26 protons in its nucleus. \n\nNow, let's go through the answer choices:\n\nA) Foreign - This choice doesn't relate to the chemical composition of the nail, so it's not the correct answer.\n\nB) Atomic 26 - This choice refers to the atomic number of Iron, which is the element represented by Fe. This is the correct answer.\n\nC) Nickel - This choice refers to a different element, not Iron (Fe). So, it's not the correct answer.\n\nD) Atomic 12 - This choice refers to an atomic number that doesn't correspond to Iron (Fe). The atomic number of Iron is 26, not 12. So, it's not the correct answer.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Atomic 26.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "fafdd566-b8c6-4095-b17d-58d3821776dc",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
