                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What does it mean if a nail is made of Fe?\n\nStep 1: Identify the meaning of \"Fe\"\nFe is the chemical symbol for the element iron.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given options\nA) foreign - This option is unrelated to the chemical symbol Fe.\nB) atomic 26 - This option refers to the atomic number of an element. We need to check if iron has an atomic number of 26.\nC) nickel - This option is another element, not related to Fe.\nD) atomic 12 - This option also refers to the atomic number of an element. We need to check if iron has an atomic number of 12.\n\nStep 3: Check the atomic number of iron\nIron (Fe) has an atomic number of 26.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer\nSince iron has an atomic number of 26, the correct answer is B) atomic 26.",
                        "answers": [
