                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what carnivores are?\n\nProfessor: Sure, carnivores are animals that require prey to survive.\n\nStudent: So, they don't eat foliage or vegetables?\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Carnivores exclusively eat meat.\n\nStudent: Are they at the bottom of the food chain?\n\nProfessor: No, actually, carnivores are usually at the top of the food chain because they are predators that hunt other animals.\n\nStudent: Do they need carbon dioxide to survive?\n\nProfessor: No, carbon dioxide is not a requirement for carnivores. They need food, water, and oxygen to survive.",
