                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question. The question is asking which statement is true about carnivores.\n\nStep 2: Recall the definition of a carnivore. A carnivore is an animal that primarily eats other animals.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate each statement based on the definition of a carnivore.\n\nA) Carnivores eat foliage and vegetables exclusively - This statement is false because carnivores primarily eat other animals, not foliage and vegetables.\n\nB) Carnivores are the bottom of the food chain - This statement is false because carnivores are usually higher up on the food chain since they eat other animals.\n\nC) Carnivores require prey to survive - This statement is true because carnivores need to eat other animals (prey) to survive.\n\nD) Carnivores require carbon dioxide to survive - This statement is false because carnivores, like all animals, require oxygen to survive, not carbon dioxide.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer based on the evaluation of each statement.\n\nThe correct answer is C) Carnivores require prey to survive.",
