                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which light appears dimmest, we need to consider the factors that affect the brightness of each light source. \n\nA) The light in the hall: This light source is likely to be relatively bright, as it is designed to illuminate a space for visibility and safety. Therefore, we can eliminate option A as the answer. \n\nB) A light in the room: The brightness of this light source will depend on the type of bulb and wattage used, as well as any lampshades or other obstructions that may affect the light output. Without more information, it is difficult to determine whether this light appears dimmer than the other options. Therefore, we cannot definitively choose option B as the answer. \n\nC) A star outside the window: Stars are typically very far away and emit relatively little light compared to artificial light sources. Therefore, it is likely that a star outside the window would appear dimmer than the other options. We can tentatively choose option C as the answer. \n\nD) A streetlight outside the window: Streetlights are designed to provide bright, even illumination for safety and visibility purposes. Therefore, it is unlikely that a streetlight would appear dimmer than the other options. We can eliminate option D as the answer. \n\nBased on this analysis, we can conclude that the light that appears dimmest is most likely option C, a star outside the window.",
