                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) Various types of animals produce pollen and seeds. \n\nReasoning: Pollen and seeds are reproductive structures of plants. While plants produce their own pollen and seeds, animals such as bees, butterflies, birds, and bats play a crucial role in pollination and seed dispersal. Therefore, option C is the correct answer. \n\nOption A is incorrect because frozen lakes do not produce pollen and seeds. Option B is incorrect because bouquets are made up of flowers, which produce pollen and seeds, but the question is asking what produces them, not what they are used for. Option D is incorrect because a person's health has no relation to the production of pollen and seeds.",
