                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure about the answer to this question. Can you help me understand it better?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through the options one by one. The question is asking about what produces pollen and seeds. Do you know what pollen and seeds are?\n\nStudent: Pollen is a powdery substance produced by plants, and seeds are the small parts of a plant that can grow into a new plant, right?\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Now, let's look at option A: lakes that are frozen over. Do you think frozen lakes can produce pollen and seeds?\n\nStudent: No, I don't think so. Lakes are bodies of water, not plants.\n\nProfessor: Good! Now, let's consider option B: things you give a loved one in a bouquet. What do you usually find in a bouquet?\n\nStudent: Flowers, I guess.\n\nProfessor: Right! And do flowers produce pollen and seeds?\n\nStudent: Yes, they do. Flowers are the reproductive parts of plants, so they produce pollen and seeds.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! Now, let's look at option C: various types of animals. Do animals produce pollen and seeds?\n\nStudent: No, animals don't produce pollen and seeds. They reproduce in different ways.\n\nProfessor: Correct! Finally, let's consider option D: a person that is healthy. Do healthy people produce pollen and seeds?\n\nStudent: No, people don't produce pollen and seeds either. They also reproduce in different ways.\n\nProfessor: Great! So, based on our discussion, which option do you think is the correct answer?\n\nStudent: I think the correct answer is B) things you give a loved one in a bouquet, because flowers produce pollen and seeds.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Well done! Do you have any other questions about this topic?\n\nStudent: No, I think I understand it now. Thank you for your help!\n\nProfessor: You're welcome! If you have any more questions in the future, don't hesitate to ask.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "baecf75f-9c53-4e67-b857-5304c19d5d28",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) things you give a loved one in a bouquet, because flowers produce pollen and seeds.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
